:[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (39 tests | 1 failed | 35 skipped) 7ms\n   ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts > MHPCO Claim Office > should quote a single staff -- premium 85 G\n     → expected [ { premium: 105 } ] to deeply equal [ { premium: 85 } ]\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 1 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯\n\n FAIL  src/claim-office.spec.ts > MHPCO Claim Office > should quote a single staff -- premium 85 G\nAssertionError: expected [ { premium: 105 } ] to deeply equal [ { premium: 85 } ]\n\n- Expected\n+ Received\n\n  Array [\n    Object {\n-     \"premium\": 85,\n+     \"premium\": 105,\n    },\n  ]\n\n ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts:47:20\n     45|       ],\n     46|     });\n     47|     expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 85 }]);\n       |                    ^\n     48|   });\n     49|   it.todo(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 45 G\");\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[1/1]⎯\n\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 3 passed | 35 todo (39)\n   Start at  01:38:51\n   Duration  155ms (transform 24ms, setup 0ms, collect 23ms, tests 7ms, environment 0ms, prepare 44ms)\n\n ELIFECYCLE  Test failed. See above for more details.\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784943531932},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Red -- Test 4: Single staff quote → premium 85 G\n\n- Activated staff test.\n- Compilation prediction: no error.\n- Runtime prediction: falls through to sword default (105 G), expected 85 G.\n\nRed Phase Complete:\n**Compilation Prediction**: No compilation error Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: Expected premium 85, received 105 Correct\n\nResult: Test fails as expected with assertion error.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:35","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi/skills/green/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":606,"output":107,"cacheRead":33984,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1,"totalTokens":34697,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943531933,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3e4310e3-5bba-4dc6-a7a9-0493bc864532","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:35","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: green\ndescription: TDD Green Phase - Implement minimal code to make the failing test pass\n---\n\n# TDD Green Phase\n\nYou are now in the **Green Phase** of TDD. Follow these instructions to make the failing test pass with MINIMAL code.\n\n## Why minimality matters\n\nThe Green Phase deliberately writes the smallest implementation that turns the active test green -- even hardcoded returns, even obviously-incomplete logic. This is not laziness or naivete:\n\n- It **exposes refactoring opportunities** in the next phase. When the implementation does exactly one thing, structural smells are visible. Over-implemented green code looks \"already clean\" and hides design problems.\n- It **prevents premature generalization**. The shape of the right abstraction emerges from the second and third test, not the first. Implementing for hypothetical future tests locks in a design before its constraints are known.\n- It **keeps the red-green-refactor cycle short**. Each cycle pays a cost in tokens and context; over-implementing in green collapses several future cycles into one large one and loses the per-test feedback loop.\n\n## Your Mission\n\n1. Implement the **minimal code** necessary to make the failing test pass\n2. Use the **simplest possible solution** (hardcoded values are acceptable)\n3. Avoid adding features for future tests\n4. Verify all tests pass\n5. NO optimization, NO refactoring yet\n\n## Context: $ARGUMENTS\n\n## Green Phase Rules\n\n- **Minimal code only**: Just enough to pass the current test\n- **Baby steps**: Make the smallest possible change\n- **No future features**: Don't implement what future tests might need\n- **Simple is better**: Hardcoded returns are perfectly fine\n- **Tests must pass**: Verify all tests are green\n- **No refactoring yet**: Save improvements for Refactor phase\n\n## Process\n\n### Step 1: Analyze the Failing Test\n\nUnderstand what the test expects:\n- What input does the test provide?\n- What output does it expect?\n- What is the **simplest** way to produce that output?\n\n### Step 2: Write Minimal Implementation\n\nImplement **only what's needed** to make the current test pass:\n\n```typescript\n// For first test \"should return 0 for empty input\":\nexport const calculate = (input: string): number => {\n  return 0; // Minimal - just make the test pass\n};\n\n// For second test \"should return number for single input\":\nexport const calculate = (input: string): number => {\n  if (input === \"\") return 0;\n  return parseInt(input); // Still simple\n};\n\n// For third test \"should add two numbers\":\nexport const calculate = (input: string): number => {\n  if (input === \"\") return 0;\n  const numbers = input.split(\",\");\n  if (numbers.length === 1) return parseInt(numbers[0]);\n  return parseInt(numbers[0]) + parseInt(numbers[1]); // Only now add logic\n};\n```\n\n### Step 3: Run Tests\n\nRun `pnpm test` and verify:\n- Current test now passes\n- All previous tests still pass\n\n### Step 4: Verify No Over-Implementation\n\nCheck yourself:\n- Did I implement features for future tests? -> Remove them\n- Did I add logic not demanded by current test? -> Remove it\n- Did I optimize prematurely? -> Simplify\n- Did I refactor existing code? -> Revert, save for Refactor phase\n\n### Step 5: Report Completion\n\n```\nGreen Phase Complete:\n**Implementation**: [brief description of what was added]\n**Result**: All tests now pass ([X] passing)\n**Approach**: [explain why this is minimal]\n\nProceeding to Refactor phase.\n```\n\n## Minimal Implementation Strategies\n\n### Hardcoded Returns (Preferred for Early Tests)\n```typescript\n// Test: \"should return 0 for empty input\"\nreturn 0; // Perfect - minimal\n```\n\n### Simple Conditionals (When Multiple Tests)\n```typescript\n// Test: \"should return number for single input\"\nif (input === \"\") return 0;\nreturn parseInt(input); // Still simple\n```\n\n### Generalization (Only When Forced)\n```typescript\n// Test: \"should add multiple numbers\" - NOW generalize\nreturn input.split(\",\").reduce((sum, n) => sum + parseInt(n), 0);\n```\n\n## Important Guidelines\n\n### DO\n- Write minimal code to make test pass\n- Use hardcoded values when appropriate\n- Take baby steps\n- Verify all tests pass\n\n### DON'T\n- Implement beyond what tests demand\n- Add features for future tests\n- Optimize prematurely\n- Refactor during Green phase\n\n## Psychological Resistance\n\nYou will feel resistance:\n- **\"This is too simple\"** -> That's correct! Minimal is the way\n- **\"Hardcoded values feel wrong\"** -> They're exactly right for early tests\n- **\"I should implement ahead\"** -> Resist this strongly\n- **\"This is inefficient\"** -> Actually accelerates development\n\nTrust the process. Simple steps compound into elegant solutions.\n\n## Completion\n\nAfter completing Green phase, proceed to Refactor phase:\n\n```\nGreen Phase Complete. Proceeding to Refactor phase.\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943532974},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Green: add staff branch. I'll add a constant and extend ternary? Minimal: add if for staff. Actually use ternary chain? Minimal is to add another condition. Let's just add staff constant and update selection. But maybe better to introduce a map? The refactor phase can do that. For green, add staff constant and nested ternary.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:36","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM = 100;\nconst AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: any): any => {\n  const items = scenario.steps[0].items;\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }];\n  }\n  const basePremium = items[0].type === \"amulet\" ? AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM : SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  return [{ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n};","newText":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM = 100;\nconst AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM = 80;\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: any): any => {\n  const items = scenario.steps[0].items;\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }];\n  }\n  const itemType = items[0].type;\n  let basePremium = SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  if (itemType === \"amulet\") {\n    basePremium = AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  } else if (itemType === \"staff\") {\n    basePremium = STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return [{ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1104,"output":438,"cacheRead":34688,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":71,"totalTokens":36230,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943532975,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-207b184d-dc4b-4498-8631-9fa3a3bba440","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:36","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"  1 const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n  2 const SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM = 100;\n  3 const AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\n+ 4 const STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM = 80;\n  4 \n  5 export const processScenario = (scenario: any): any => {\n  6   const items = scenario.steps[0].items;\n  7   if (items.length === 0) {\n  8     return [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }];\n  9   }\n-10   const basePremium = items[0].type === \"amulet\" ? AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM : SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM;\n+11   const itemType = items[0].type;\n+12   let basePremium = SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM;\n+13   if (itemType === \"amulet\") {\n+14     basePremium = AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM;\n+15   } else if (itemType === \"staff\") {\n+16     basePremium = STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM;\n+17   }\n 11   return [{ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n 12 };","patch":"--- src/claim-office.ts\n+++ src/claim-office.ts\n@@ -1,12 +1,19 @@\n const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n const SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM = 100;\n const AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\n+const STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM = 80;\n \n export const processScenario = (scenario: any): any => {\n   const items = scenario.steps[0].items;\n   if (items.length === 0) {\n     return [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }];\n   }\n-  const basePremium = items[0].type === \"amulet\" ? AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM : SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM;\n+  const itemType = items[0].type;\n+  let basePremium = SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM;\n+  if (itemType === \"amulet\") {\n+    basePremium = AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM;\n+  } else if (itemType === \"staff\") {\n+    basePremium = STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM;\n+  }\n   return [{ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n };\n","firstChangedLine":4},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943535111},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Run tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:37","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test 2>&1","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":36,"output":32,"cacheRead":36224,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4,"totalTokens":36292,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943535115,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl