e","timestamp":1784943536592,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-5dea0f27-0647-4b4a-837a-194664fc6039","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:38","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Consolidated the item-type-to-base-premium mapping from an `if/else` chain into a declarative `BASE_PREMIUMS` lookup table.\n- Replaced three individual base-premium constants (`SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM`, `AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM`, `STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM`) with one map.\n- Preserved the existing default-to-sword behavior for unknown types via `?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword`.\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- `processScenario` still fits: it processes a scenario and returns results.\n- `BASE_PREMIUMS` clearly reveals intent: a table of base premiums by item type.\n- No function renames were needed.\n\n**APP Mass Calculation**:\n\n*Before (initial implementation)*:\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM = 100;\nconst AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM = 80;\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: any): any => {\n  const items = scenario.steps[0].items;\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }];\n  }\n  const itemType = items[0].type;\n  let basePremium = SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  if (itemType === \"amulet\") {\n    basePremium = AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  } else if (itemType === \"staff\") {\n    basePremium = STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return [{ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n};\n```\n- Constants: 8  → 8\n- Bindings: 4  → 4\n- Invocations: 4 (`===` x3, `+` x1) → 8\n- Conditionals: 3 → 12\n- Loops: 0 → 0\n- Assignments: 5 → 30\n- **Total Mass: 62**\n\n*After (refactored implementation)*:\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: any): any => {\n  const items = scenario.steps[0].items;\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }];\n  }\n  const basePremium = BASE_PREMIUMS[items[0].type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n  return [{ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n};\n```\n- Constants: 8 → 8\n- Bindings: 3 → 3\n- Invocations: 2 (`===`, `+`) → 4\n- Conditionals: 2 (`if`, `??`) → 8\n- Loops: 0 → 0\n- Assignments: 2 → 12\n- **Total Mass: 35**\n\n**Mass Change**: 62 → 35 (reduced by 27)\n\n**Simple Design Rules Applied**:\n1. **Tests Pass**: All 4 active tests continue to pass; 35 tests remain todo.\n2. **Reveals Intent**: The lookup table makes the type-to-premium relationship explicit and self-documenting.\n3. **No Duplication**: Removed the repeated `basePremium = ...` assignment pattern; each premium value now has a single representation.\n4. **Fewest Elements**: Replaced three conditionals and five assignments with one lookup and one fallback.\n\n**Tests**: `pnpm test` — 4 passed, 35 todo, all green."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 4\nRecent Green phase: Added staff base premium constant and branch.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 4\nRecent Green phase: Added staff base premium constant and branch.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"tim