plicit.\n\n## Current Code Mass (before)\n\n```typescript\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: any): any => {\n  const items = scenario.steps[0].items;\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }];\n  }\n  const basePremium = BASE_PREMIUMS[items[0].type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n  return [{ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n};\n```\n\n- Constants: 6 (`5`, `100`, `60`, `80`, `40`, `0`) → 6\n- Bindings: 3 (`scenario`, `items`, `basePremium`) → 3\n- Invocations: 1 (`+`) → 2\n- Conditionals: 2 (`if`, `??`) → 8\n- Loops: 0 → 0\n- Assignments: 0 → 0\n\n**Total Mass: 19**\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\nExtracted two small, intent-revealing helpers:\n\n```typescript\nconst basePremiumFor = (item: any): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n\nconst buildQuote = (items: any[]): any[] => {\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }];\n  }\n  return [{ premium: basePremiumFor(items[0]) + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: any): any =>\n  buildQuote(scenario.steps[0].items);\n```\n\n**Why this is an improvement (Rule 2 clarity):**\n- `processScenario` now reads as \"build a quote from the scenario's step items\".\n- `basePremiumFor` isolates the item-to-base-premium mapping, including the current default-to-sword behavior.\n- `buildQuote` isolates quote construction, making future additions (multi-item logic, surcharges, discounts) easier to place.\n\n## New Code Mass (after)\n\n- Constants: 6 → 6\n- Bindings: 3 (`item`, `items`, `scenario`) → 3\n- Invocations: 3 (`basePremiumFor`, `+`, `buildQuote`) → 6\n- Conditionals: 2 (`if`, `??`) → 8\n- Loops: 0 → 0\n- Assignments: 0 → 0\n\n**Total Mass: 23**\n\n**Mass Change**: 19 → 23 (+4)\n\nThe mass increased slightly because explicit function calls replaced inline nesting. This is acceptable under Rule 2 (Reveals Intent), which takes priority over APP mass.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll tests pass:\n\n```\nTest Files  1 pas