functions.subagent:54","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 6\nRecent Green phase: Added rune entry to BASE_PREMIUMS map.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","cwd":"."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":262,"output":193,"cacheRead":44032,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":44487,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943620443,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-00b728c8-1228-47d9-ae10-8f2b1adb5cc7","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:54","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring complete.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Added TypeScript domain interfaces (`Item`, `QuoteStep`, `Scenario`) to replace `any` annotations.\n- `item: any` → `item: Item`\n- `items: any[]` → `items: Item[]`\n- `scenario: any` → `scenario: Scenario`\n- Added explicit return types (`Array<{ premium: number }>`) for `buildQuote` and `processScenario`.\n- Added index signature `[key: string]: unknown` to `Item` so test objects with extra properties (`material`, `enchantment`, `cursed`) remain valid under strict mode.\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- `PROCESSING_FEE` and `BASE_PREMIUMS`: clear, kept.\n- `basePremiumFor`: describes lookup intent; fallback behavior will likely be revisited when unknown-type rejection tests are activated, so kept as-is.\n- `buildQuote` and `processScenario`: names match current responsibilities, kept.\n\n**APP Mass Calculation**:\n\n*Before*:\n```\nConstants:  6 (5, 100, 60, 80, 40, 25) = 6\nBindings:   3 (item, items, scenario)    = 3\nInvocations:2 (basePremiumFor, buildQuote)= 4\nConditionals:1 (if items.length === 0)   = 4\nLoops:      0                           = 0\nAssignments:0                           = 0\nTotal Mass: 17\n```\n\n*After*:\n```\nConstants:  6  = 6\nBindings:   3  = 3\nInvocations:2  = 4\nConditionals:1  = 4\nLoops:      0  = 0\nAssignments:0  = 0\nTotal Mass: 17\n```\n\nMass change: `17 -> 17` (no delta). Type annotations do not add runtime mass.\n\n**Simple Design Rules**:\n1. Tests pass: ✅ All 6 passing tests remain green; `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit` also passes.\n2. Reveals intent: ✅ `any` replaced with domain types; code now self-documents the expected scenario/quote shape.\n3. No duplication: ✅ No duplicated logic to extract.\n4. Fewest elements: ✅ No unnecessary abstractions added; implementation remains minimal.\n\n**Tests**: All passing (`6 passed | 33 todo`)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 6\nRecent Green phase: Added rune entry to BASE_PREMIUMS map.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 6\nRecent Green phase: Added rune entry to BASE_PREMIUMS map.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784943622143},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to act as the refactor subagent. I need to:\n1. Read the implementation file and test file\n2. Evaluate naming first\n3. Calculate APP mass before and after\n4. Apply Simple Design Rules in priority order\n5. Keep tests green\n6. Attempt at least one refactoring\n7. Document decisions\n\nLet me start by reading the files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":82,"output":117,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":79,"totalTokens":6215,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943622164,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-48e305e7-0f53-4ab4-93fb-cbcf2224058f","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (item: any): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n\nconst buildQuote = (items: any[]): any[] => {\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }];\n  }\n  return [{ premium: basePremiumFor(items[0]) + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: any): any =>\n  buildQuote(scenario.steps[0].items);\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943623010},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quote premiums\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 105 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 65 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 65 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 85 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"oak\", enchantment: 1, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 85 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 45 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 45 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 30 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 30 }]);\n  });\n  it.todo(