3. **No duplication** — eliminated the unused duplicate fallback in `basePremiumFor`.\n4. **Fewest elements** — removed one unused function."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 13\nRecent Green phase: Replaced rune-only block check with grouped component counting applying the 60 G block per component type when count is 3.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 13\nRecent Green phase: Replaced rune-only block check with grouped component counting applying the 60 G block per component type when count is 3.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784943798406},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the implementation and test files to understand what we're working with.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":96,"output":56,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":18,"totalTokens":6168,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943798427,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-fcbeeacd-fbfc-4319-abcc-c39e4d87d278","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst RUNE_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst RUNE_BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  [key: string]: unknown;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: string;\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: QuoteStep[];\n}\n\ntype Quote = Array<{ premium: number }>;\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (item: Item): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\";\n\nconst componentBasePremium = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  isComponent(type) && count === RUNE_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? RUNE_BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM\n    : count * (BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword);\n\nconst buildQuoteFor = (items: Item[]): Quote => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  });\n  let baseTotal = 0;\n  counts.forEach((count, type) => {\n    baseTotal += componentBasePremium(type, count);\n  });\n  return [{ premium: baseTotal + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Quote =>\n  buildQuoteFor(scenario.steps[0].items);\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943799121},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quote premiums\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 105 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 65 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 65 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 85 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"oak\", enchantment: 1, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 85 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 45 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 45 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 30 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 30 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single moonstone -- premium 30 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 30 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Component block rules\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes without block discount -- premium 55 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 55 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote exactly 3 runes with block discount -- premium 65 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 65 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 105 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 180 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 180 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not mix different component types for the block discount -- 2 runes + 1 moonstone premium 80 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 80 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply separate blocks for each component type -- 3 runes + 3 moonstones premium 125 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 125 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it.todo(\"should add cursed surcharge to a sword -- premium 155 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at level 5 -- premium 135 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should add both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges -- premium 185 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge below level 5 -- premium 105 G\");\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 85 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply first insurance surcharge -- premium 115 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply follow-up contract discount -- premium 90 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply item-specific modifiers per item and policy-wide modifiers on policy base -- cursed sword + plain amulet premium 215 G\");\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it.todo(\"should compute newcomer with a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute long-standing customer's second contract -- premium 160 G\");\n\n  // Claim standard reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G, remaining cap 1600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse a rune damage minus deductible -- payout 100 G, remaining cap 400 G\");\n\n  // Claim special clauses\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage minus deductible -- payout 700 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should halve damage for enchantment level 9 or higher -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply enchantment clause over dragon material when both apply -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply dragon-material clause when only it applies -- payout 700 G\");\n\n  // Multi-item / deductible\n  it.todo(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident -- total payout 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should sum insurance values for multiple items of the same type -- cap 4000 G\");\n\n  // Cap exhaustion\n  it.todo(\"should cap the first claim and track remaining cap -- first payout 1400 G, remaining 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should reduce the second claim by remaining cap -- second payout 600 G, remaining 0 G\");\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 7 runes with first insurance yields 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- high-enchantment damage 901 G yields 350 G\");\n\n  // Error cases\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in quote\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in claim\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject negative damage amount\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject more damages than insured items\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943799121},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me run the tests first to confirm they're green, then I'll do the refactoring analysis.\n\nCurrent code analysis:\n1. Naming:\n   - `isComponent`: checks if type is \"rune\" or \"moonstone\" - the name is okay but could be more specific\n   - `componentBasePremium`: calculates premium for a type based on count. The name suggests it only handles components but it handles all types. The function uses a conditional for block discount. This name doesn't fit perfectly.\n   - `Rune_BLOCK_SIZE`, `RUNE_BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM`: These constants are specific to runes but apply to moonstones too. Misleading.\n   - `BASE_PREMIUMS`: Good name.\n   - `basePremiumFor`: Returns base premium for an item, but it's only used potentially - actually it's not used! Let me check.\n   - `buildQuoteFor`: Builds a quote from items. Good.\n\nActually `basePremiumFor` is not used at all in `buildQuoteFor`. Let me verify:\n- `componentBasePremium` uses `BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword`\n- `basePremiumFor` is defined but never called\n\nSo there's an unused function. That's an opportunity under Rule 4.\n\n2. Duplication:\n- `BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword` appears in both `basePremiumFor` and `componentBasePremium` (though basePremiumFor is unused)\n- The constants `RUNE_BLOCK_SIZE` and `RUNE_BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM` are misleading because they apply to both runes and moonstones.\n\n3. Fewest elements:\n- `basePremiumFor` is unused, can remove\n- Could consolidate constants naming\n\nLet me first run tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":2377,"output":400,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":376,"totalTokens":8921,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943799121,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-396a5dd6-32af-4499-b7a9-08b97d65cb42","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-