ript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","cwd":"."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":236,"output":203,"cacheRead":67456,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":67895,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943858514,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e6349570-02d7-4d18-8cd1-d929f96e4c2b","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:101","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring complete. All 14 passing tests still pass (`25` remain todo).\n\n**Refactoring Applied to `src/claim-office.ts`**\n\n1. **Naming**\n   - `buildQuoteFor` → `quoteForItems` — clearly states it produces a quote from a list of items.\n   - `basePremiumForTypeGroup` → `basePremiumForGroup` — symmetric with the new `basePremiumForItem` helper.\n\n2. **Eliminated duplication (DRY)**\n   - Extracted `basePremiumForItem(type)` so the “fall back to sword premium” rule lives in one place instead of being repeated in the group premium and curse surcharge calculations.\n\n3. **Replaced magic number**\n   - Added `CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5` to name the 50% curse surcharge.\n\n4. **Removed mutable accumulators**\n   - Replaced `let baseTotal` / `let itemSurcharges` plus `if` / `+=` with `reduce`-based sums, making the “sum of group premiums” and “sum of curse surcharges” intents explicit.\n\n**APP Mass Calculation** (counted via a small AST script)\n\n| Component | Before | After |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Constants | 17 | 17 |\n| Bindings | 21 | 24 |\n| Invocations | 9 | 13 |\n| Conditionals | 2 | 2 |\n| Loops | 3 | 3 |\n| Assignments | 2 | 0 |\n| **Total Mass** | **91** | **90** |\n\nMass dropped by **1**; the main structural win is removing mutable assignments (`+=`) while keeping loops and conditionals flat.\n\n**Simple Design Check**\n\n- **Rule 1 — Tests pass:** ✅ `pnpm test` → `14 passed | 25 todo`\n- **Rule 2 — Reveals intent:** ✅ function names describe what they return; named constants replace magic numbers\n- **Rule 3 — No duplication:** ✅ single `basePremiumForItem` for the unknown-type fallback\n- **Rule 4 — Fewest elements:** ✅ removed mutable `let` accumulators and the `if` statement; kept only one small extra helper\n\nFinal implementation in `src/claim-office.ts` is green and ready for the next test."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 14\nRecent Green phase: Added per-item curse surcharge of 50% of base premium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 14\nRecent Green phase: Added per-item curse surcharge of 50% of base premium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784943861027},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need act as refactor subagent? User gave task to refactor implementation, test file src/claim-office.spec.ts, impl src/claim-office.ts, passing tests 14, recent green added per-item curse surcharge of 50% of base premium. We must refactor keeping tests green. Need read files, run tests, apply simple design, calculate APP mass before/after, document decisions. Need use tools. We are in cwd. Need inspect files. Also possibly have skill context? We are subagent? We can read AGENTS.md? Already have project context. Need follow refactoring rules. Mandatory attempt. Need calculate mass. Let's start reading implementation and tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":83,"output":194,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":135,"totalTokens":6293,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943861047,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-51504305-9b9c-4f76-b68a-d47f5b42acce","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  [key: string]: unknown;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: string;\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: QuoteStep[];\n}\n\ntype Quote = Array<{ premium: number }>;\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\";\n\nconst basePremiumForTypeGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  isComponent(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * (BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword);\n\nconst buildQuoteFor = (items: Item[]): Quote => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  });\n  let baseTotal = 0;\n  counts.forEach((count, type) => {\n    baseTotal += basePremiumForTypeGroup(type, count);\n  });\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemSurcharges += 0.5 * (BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword);\n    }\n  });\n  return [{ premium: baseTotal + itemSurcharges + PROCESSING_FEE }];\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Quote =>\n  buildQuoteFor(scenario.steps[0].items);\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943862976},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quote premiums\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 105 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 65 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 65 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 85 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"oak\", enchantment: 1, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 85 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 45 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 45 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 30 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 30 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single moonstone -- premium 30 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 30 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Component block rules\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes without block discount -- premium 55 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 55 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote exactly 3 runes with block discount -- premium 65 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 65 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 105 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 180 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 180 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not mix different component types for the block discount -- 2 runes + 1 moonstone premium 80 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 80 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply separate blocks for each component type -- 3 runes + 3 moonstones premium 125 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 125 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should add cursed surcharge to a sword -- premium 155 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 155 }]);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at level 5 -- premium 135 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should add both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges -- premium 185 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge below level 5 -- premium 105 G\");\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 85 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply first insurance surcharge -- premium 115 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply follow-up contract discount -- premium 90 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply item-specific modifiers per item and policy-wide modifiers on policy base -- cursed sword + plain amulet premium 215 G\");\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it.todo(\"should compute newcomer with a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute long-standing customer's second contract -- premium 160 G\");\n\n  // Claim standard reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G, remaining cap 1600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse a rune damage minus deductible -- payout 100 G, remaining cap 400 G\");\n\n  // Claim special clauses\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage minus deductible -- payout 700 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should halve damage for enchantment level 9 or higher -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply enchantment clause over dragon material when both apply -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply dragon-material clause when only it applies -- payout 700 G\");\n\n  // Multi-item / deductible\n  it.todo(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident -- total payout 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should sum insurance values for multiple items of the same type -- cap 4000 G\");\n\n  // Cap exhaustion\n  it.todo(\"should cap the first claim and track remaining cap -- first payout 1400 G, remaining 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should reduce the second claim by remaining cap -- second payout 600 G, remaining 0 G\");\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 7 runes with first insurance yields 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- high-enchantment damage 901 G yields 350 G\");\n\n  // Error cases\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in quote\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in claim\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject negative damage amount\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject more damages than insured items\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943862976},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (39 tests | 25 skipped) 3ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  14 passed | 25 todo (39)\n   Start at  01:44:22\n   Duration  158ms (transform 31ms, setup 0ms, collect 29ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943862976},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We have implementation with 14 passing tests. Need evaluate naming, apply refactoring. The implementation is minimal, but could be improved. Let's analyze code.\n\n```\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  