openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":252,"output":204,"cacheRead":71488,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":71944,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943994938,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-4255daee-9910-4756-a5d1-b55fb9e24926","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:109","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring Complete.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n1. **Naming / Intent (`Item` interface)**: Replaced the overly-permissive index signature `[key: string]: unknown` with explicit optional fields (`cursed`, `enchantment`, `material`, `damage`). This reveals what attributes an item can actually carry and improves TypeScript type safety.\n2. **Extract `surchargeForItem`**: Isolated the cursed + high-enchantment surcharge logic into a named helper. This removes the duplicated \"rate × base\" pattern inside `quoteForItems` and makes the surcharge rule self-documenting.\n\n**APP Mass Calculation**:\n- **Initial total mass**: 107\n  - `isComponent`: 7\n  - `basePremiumForItem`: 5\n  - `basePremiumForGroup`: 11\n  - `quoteForItems`: 81\n  - `processScenario`: 3\n- **Refactored total mass**: 121\n  - `isComponent`: 7\n  - `basePremiumForItem`: 5\n  - `basePremiumForGroup`: 11\n  - `surchargeForItem`: 35\n  - `quoteForItems`: 60\n  - `processScenario`: 3\n- **Mass change**: 107 → 121 (+14)\n\n**Why mass increased**:\nThe new `surchargeForItem` helper adds a function boundary, which adds bindings, assignments, and invocations. However, Simple Design Rules 2 (reveals intent) and 3 (no duplication) outrank Rule 4 / APP mass. The surcharge logic now has a single, named representation, making future changes (e.g., adding a new item modifier) localized and obvious.\n\n**Tests**: All 15 passing tests remain green; 24 tests still todo.\n\n**Verification**:\n- `pnpm test` ✅\n