":"text","text":"## Green -- Test 19: First insurance surcharge + premium rounding up\n\nAdded 10 % first-insurance surcharge on policy base and `Math.ceil` final premium. Updated earlier base-premium tests to include first insurance and rounding.\n\nGreen Phase Complete:\n**Implementation**: Added first insurance surcharge and final premium rounding up\n**Result**: All tests pass (19 passing, 20 todo)\n**Approach**: Applied global policy-wide surcharge and rounding as required by spec\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.subagent:135","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Added first insurance surcharge and Math.ceil rounding; updated earlier base tests to include first insurance.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","cwd":"."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":275,"output":300,"cacheRead":93440,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":84,"totalTokens":94015,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944138712,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-bd36ec39-2b42-4d42-b2db-d83751579e30","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:135","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Refactoring Complete**\n\n### Tests\nAll tests pass before and after the refactoring:\n- **Before:** 19 passed, 20 todo\n- **After:** 19 passed, 20 todo\n\n---\n\n### Naming Evaluation (Rule 2 — Reveals Intent)\n\n| Name | Purpose | Assessment | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `processScenario` | Entry point for processing a customer scenario | Generic, but the spec clearly has broader scenarios (claims, multiple steps); acceptable as the umbrella name | Keep |\n| `quoteForItems` | Builds a quote premium for a list of items | Accurate | Keep |\n| `counts` | Map of item type → quantity | Too vague; doesn't reveal that it's a per-type quantity | **Rename to `quantityByType`** |\n| `premium` (final local) | Unrounded premium before `Math.ceil` | Confusing because the returned property is also called `premium` but is the rounded value | **Rename to `rawPremium`** |\n| `surchargeForItem` | Computes cursed + enchantment surcharges | OK, but the two internal surcharge calculations repeat the same \"if condition then base × rate\" pattern | **Extract `surchargeWhen`** |\n\n---\n\n### APP Mass Calculation\n\nCounting methodology: numeric literals as constants; function parameters and local `const` identifiers as bindings; function/method calls as invocations; `?:` as conditionals; `forEach`/`reduce` as loops; `const` declarations and `Map.set` as assignments.\n\n#### Before Refactoring\n```typescript\n// original claim-office.ts\n```\n\n| Component | Count | Mass |\n|---|---|---|\n| Constants | 19 | 19 |\n| Bindings | 24 | 24 |\n| Invocations | 12 | 24 |\n| Conditionals | 4 | 16 |\n| Loops | 3 | 15 |\n| Assignments | 7 | 42 |\n| **Total** | | **140** |\n\n#### After Refactoring\n```typescript\n// refactored claim-office.ts\n```\n\n| Component | Count | Mass |\n|---|---|---|\n| Constants | 19 | 19 |\n| Bindings | 25 | 25 |\n| Invocations | 14 | 28 |\n| Conditionals | 3 | 12 |\n| Loops | 3 | 15 |\n| Assignments | 5 | 30 |\n| **Total** | | **129** |\n\n**Mass Change:** `140 → 129` (reduction of **11**)\n\n---\n\n### Refactorings Applied\n\n1. **Grouped all policy constants at the top**  \n   Moved `LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE`, `LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD`, and `FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE` together with the other rate/threshold constants. This removes a jarring interruption between `surchargeForItem` and `quoteForItems`.\n\n2. **Extracted `surchargeWhen` helper**  \n   Captured the repeated \"if condition applies, charge `base × rate`\" pattern used by both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges. This removes conceptual duplication and makes `surchargeForItem` read as a simple sum of two conditional surcharges.\n\n3. **Renamed `counts` → `quantityByType`**  \n   The map now clearly communicates that it holds per-item-type quantities.\n\n4. **Renamed final `premium` → `rawPremium`**  \n   Distinguishes the pre-rounded value from the rounded `premium` returned in the `Quote`.\n\n---\n\n### Simple Design Rules Check\n\n| Rule | Status |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Tests pass | ✅ All 19 tests still pass |\n| 2. Reveals intent | ✅ Better names (`quantityByType`, `rawPremium`, `surchargeWhen`) and grouped constants |\n| 3. No duplication | ✅ `surchargeWhen` removes repeated conditional-rate logic |\n| 4. Fewest elements | Net +1 helper function, but lower mass and clearer intent; trade-off justified |\n\n---\n\n**Refactoring**: Applied 4 targeted improvements (constant grouping, `surchargeWhen` extraction, and two renames).  \n**Mass Change**: `140 → 129` (-11).  \n**Tests**: All passing."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Added first insurance surcharge and Math.ceil rounding; updated earlier base tests to include first insurance.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Added first insurance surcharge and Math.ceil rounding; updated earlier base tests to include first insurance.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784944141629},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the implementation and test files to understand what we're working with.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":88,"output":144,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":18,"totalTokens":6248,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944141649,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3c7a0213-d3f0-4b80-a084-c0cea924bdec","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n  damage?: number;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: string;\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: QuoteStep[];\n}\n\ntype Quote = Array<{ premium: number }>;\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\";\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (type: string): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n\nconst basePremiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  isComponent(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * basePremiumForItem(type);\n\nconst surchargeForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item.type);\n  const cursedSurcharge = item.cursed ? CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE * base : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    typeof item.enchantment === \"number\" && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE * base\n      : 0;\n  return cursedSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst quoteForItems = (items: Item[], customerYears: number): Quote => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  });\n\n  const baseTotal = Array.from(counts.entries()).reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + basePremiumForGroup(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce(\n    (total, item) => total + surchargeForItem(item),\n    0\n  );\n\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customerYears >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD\n      ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE * baseTotal\n      : 0;\n\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE * baseTotal;\n\n  const policyBase = baseTotal + itemSurcharges;\n  const premium = policyBase - loyaltyDiscount + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return [{ premium: Math.ceil(premium) }];\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Quote =>\n  quoteForItems(scenario.steps[0].items, scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO);\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944142543},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quote premiums\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"oak\", enchantment: 1, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 93 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 49 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single moonstone -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Component block rules\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes without block discount -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 60 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote exactly 3 runes with block discount -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 198 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not mix different component types for the block discount -- 2 runes + 1 moonstone premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 88 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply separate blocks for each component type -- 3 runes + 3 moonstones premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 137 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should add cursed surcharge to a sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 165 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at level 5 -- premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges -- premium 195 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 195 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge below level 5 -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply first insurance surcharge -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should apply follow-up contract discount -- premium 90 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply item-specific modifiers per item and policy-wide modifiers on policy base -- cursed sword + plain amulet premium 215 G\");\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it.todo(\"should compute newcomer with a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute long-standing customer's second contract -- premium 160 G\");\n\n  // Claim standard reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G, remaining cap 1600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse a rune damage minus deductible -- payout 100 G, remaining cap 400 G\");\n\n  // Claim special clauses\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage minus deductible -- payout 700 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should halve damage for enchantment level 9 or higher -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply enchantment clause over dragon material when both apply -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply dragon-material clause when only it applies -- payout 700 G\");\n\n  // Multi-item / deductible\n  it.todo(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident -- total payout 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should sum insurance values for multiple items of the same type -- cap 4000 G\");\n\n  // Cap exhaustion\n  it.todo(\"should cap the first claim and track remaining cap -- first payout 1400 G, remaining 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should reduce the second claim by remaining cap -- second payout 600 G, remaining 0 G\");\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 7 runes with first insurance yields 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- high-enchantment damage 901 G yields 350 G\");\n\n  // Error cases\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in quote\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in claim\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject negative damage amount\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject more damages than insured items\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944142543},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me run tests first to verify all 19 tests pass. Then I'll evaluate naming and apply simple design rules.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7 && pnpm test","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":3207,"output":96,"cacheRead":6208,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":24,"totalTokens":9511,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944142544,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-571965a1-46dc-464e-9304-19c8ae63f5e6","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (39 tests | 20 skipped) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  19 passed | 20 todo (39)\n   Start at  01:49:04\n   Duration  156ms (transform 31ms, setup 0ms, collect 29ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944144317},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 19 tests pass. Now I'll evaluate the code.\n\n**Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY):**\n\nCurrent names and their purposes:\n- `isComponent`: checks if item type is rune or moonstone. Good.\n- `basePremiumForItem`: returns base premium for item type, with fallback to sword. OK but maybe `basePremiumForItemType`? Hmm, probably fine.\n- `basePremiumForGroup`: calculates base premium for a group of same-type items. OK.\n- `surchargeForItem`: calculates surcharge for an item based on cursed/high-enchantment. Good.\n- `quoteForItems`: builds a quote for a list of items given customer years. OK.\n- `processScenario`: processes the entire scenario. Good.\n\nLooking at `processScenario` - it currently only processes `scenario.steps[0].items` and assumes `op` is \"quote\". The name \"processScenario\" is a bit generic. But given the current tests, it only handles quote operations. However, there are many todo tests about claims, so eventually it will need to handle claim operations too. The name is probably OK for now.\n\nWait, let me look at the implementation more carefully. There are some issues:\n\n1. `processScenario` only processes `scenario.steps[0].items` - it ignores the operation type and any other steps. But for the current tests this works.\n\n2. `quoteForItems` does item counting with `Map`. This is fine.\n\n3. `surchargeForItem` uses `basePremiumForItem(item.type)` but the first insurance and loyalty are based on `baseTotal` which is group-based. This matches the tests.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the implementation, I notice potential naming clarity issues:\n\n- `COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM` = 60. This is a constant for the price of 3 components (block size). Could be clearer but OK.\n- The `counts` map is created but then `Array.from(counts.entries()).reduce(...)`. This could be simplified with a for...of loop or using Map.forEach.\n\nLet me think about duplication and intent issues:\n\n**Duplication**: \n- `counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);` - fine\n- `Array.from(counts.entries()).reduce((total, [type, count]) => total + basePremiumForGroup(type, count), 0);` - this reduce pattern\n- `items.reduce((total, item) => total + surchargeForItem(item), 0);` - similar reduce pattern\n\nCould extract a `sum` helper but that might add abstraction.\n\nActually, the two reduce calls have conceptual duplication - both sum over collections. But extracting a generic `sum` function might not improve clarity much in T