{"type":"text","text":"Tests remain green after the refactor.\n\n## Refactored Code Mass (approximate)\n\n| Function | Mass |\n|---|---|\n| `isComponent` | 3 |\n| `basePremiumForItem` | 1 |\n| `basePremiumForGroup` | 11 |\n| `surchargeWhen` | 8 |\n| `surchargeForItem` | ~18 |\n| `basePremiumTotal` | ~52 |\n| `policyAdjustment` | ~36 |\n| `quoteForItems` | ~48 |\n| `processScenario` | ~13 |\n\n**Total after: ~190**\n\n## Mass Change\n\n**Before: ~189 → After: ~190** (delta: ~+1)\n\nMass increased negligibly due to function-declaration and call-site overhead.\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n**Rule 2 — Reveals Intent (priority)**\n\nExtracted two named functions from `quoteForItems`:\n\n1. **`basePremiumTotal(items)`** — encapsulates the quantity-grouping and component block-discount logic.\n2. **`policyAdjustment(baseTotal, customerYears, isFollowUp)`** — encapsulates the net effect of policy-wide modifiers (loyalty discount, first-insurance surcharge, follow-up discount).\n\nThis makes `quoteForItems` read as a clear formula:\n\n```ts\nconst policyBase = baseTotal + itemSurcharges;\nconst rawPremium = policyBase + policyAdjustment(...) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n```\n\n**Rule 3 — No Duplication:** No duplicated logic existed; extraction created single representations for the two concepts above.\n\n**Rule 4 — Fewest Elements:** No unnecessary abstractions were removed or added; the two new helpers directly correspond to distinct business concepts.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe small APP-mass increase is acceptable because Rule 2 (clarity) trumps mass. The code now more clearly reveals the separate concerns of base-premium calculation, item surcharges, policy-wide adjustments, and final premium assembly.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n- **Refactoring:** Extracted `basePremiumTotal` and `policyAdjustment` to clarify responsibilities in `quoteForItems`\n- **Mass Change:** ~189 → ~190 (negligible increase)\n- **Tests:** All 20 passing, 19 todo unchanged"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Enabled multi-step processing with flatMap and added follow-up discount for non-first quote steps.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Enabled multi-step processing with flatMap and added follow-up discount for non-first quote steps.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784944245287},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to refactor the claim-office implementation. I need to:\n1. Read the test file and implementation file\n2. Evaluate naming first\n3. Calculate APP mass before\n4. Apply Simple Design Rules in priority order\n5. Make at least one refactoring\n6. Keep tests green\n7. Calculate APP mass after\n8. Document decisions\n\nLet me start by reading the files and running tests to see current state.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll refactor the claim-office implementation. Let me start by reading the relevant files and verifying tests are green."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":88,"output":170,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":90,"totalTokens":6274,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944245307,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-39ac2535-bd8e-450f-8066-4b4a81a7237c","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n  damage?: number;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: string;\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: QuoteStep[];\n}\n\ntype Quote = Array<{ premium: number }>;\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\";\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (type: string): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n\nconst basePremiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  isComponent(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * basePremiumForItem(type);\n\nconst surchargeWhen = (applies: boolean, base: number, rate: number): number =>\n  applies ? base * rate : 0;\n\nconst surchargeForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item.type);\n  return (\n    surchargeWhen(item.cursed ?? false, base, CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE) +\n    surchargeWhen(\n      typeof item.enchantment === \"number\" && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n      base,\n      HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    )\n  );\n};\n\nconst quoteForItems = (items: Item[], customerYears: number, isFollowUp: boolean): Quote => {\n  const quantityByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    quantityByType.set(item.type, (quantityByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  });\n\n  const baseTotal = Array.from(quantityByType.entries()).reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + basePremiumForGroup(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce(\n    (total, item) => total + surchargeForItem(item),\n    0\n  );\n\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customerYears >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD\n      ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE * baseTotal\n      : 0;\n\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE * baseTotal;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFollowUp ? FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE * baseTotal : 0;\n\n  const policyBase = baseTotal + itemSurcharges;\n  const rawPremium = policyBase - loyaltyDiscount + firstInsuranceSurcharge - followUpDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return [{ premium: Math.ceil(rawPremium) }];\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Quote =>\n  scenario.steps.flatMap((step, index) =>\n    quoteForItems(step.items, scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, index > 0)\n  );\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944246964},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quote premiums\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"oak\", enchantment: 1, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 93 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 49 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single moonstone -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Component block rules\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes without block discount -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 60 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote exactly 3 runes with block discount -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 198 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not mix different component types for the block discount -- 2 runes + 1 moonstone premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 88 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply separate blocks for each component type -- 3 runes + 3 moonstones premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 137 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should add cursed surcharge to a sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 165 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at level 5 -- premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges -- premium 195 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 195 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge below level 5 -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply first insurance surcharge -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on the second quote -- premium 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }, { premium: 100 }]);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should apply item-specific modifiers per item and policy-wide modifiers on policy base -- cursed sword + plain amulet premium 215 G\");\n\n  // In