xpected [ { premium: 145 }, …(1) ] to deeply equal [ { premium: 145 }, …(1) ]\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 1 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯\n\n FAIL  src/claim-office.spec.ts > MHPCO Claim Office > should halve damage for enchantment level 9 or higher -- payout 400 G\nAssertionError: expected [ { premium: 145 }, …(1) ] to deeply equal [ { premium: 145 }, …(1) ]\n\n- Expected\n+ Received\n\n  Array [\n    Object {\n      \"premium\": 145,\n    },\n    Object {\n-     \"payout\": 400,\n-     \"remainingCap\": 1600,\n+     \"payout\": 900,\n+     \"remainingCap\": 1100,\n    },\n  ]\n\n ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts:385:20\n    383|       ],\n    384|     });\n    385|     expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remaining…\n       |                    ^\n    386|   });\n    387|   it.todo(\"should apply enchantment clause over dragon material when b…\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[1/1]⎯\n\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 26 passed | 12 todo (39)\n   Start at  01:53:10\n   Duration  169ms (transform 34ms, setup 0ms, collect 33ms, tests 9ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n ELIFECYCLE  Test failed. See above for more details.\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784944391072},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Red -- Test 27: High-enchantment (level 9) damage → payout 400 G\n\n- Activated high-enchantment claim test.\n- Compilation prediction: no error.\n- Runtime prediction: standard reimbursement (1000 - 100 = 900), expected halved (1000/2 - 100 = 400).\n\nRed Phase Complete:\n**Compilation Prediction**: No compilation error Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: Expected payout 400, received 900 Correct\n\nResult: Test fails as expected with assertion error.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:174","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi/skills/green/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":625,"output":131,"cacheRead":119616,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1,"totalTokens":120372,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944391075,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-947323c4-5dec-4b3d-9930-0446bdf6a4f2","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:174","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: green\ndescription: TDD Green Phase - Implement minimal code to make the failing test pass\n---\n\n# TDD Green Phase\n\nYou are now in the **Green Phase** of TDD. Follow these instructions to make the failing test pass with MINIMAL code.\n\n## Why minimality matters\n\nThe Green Phase deliberately writes the smallest implementation that turns the active test green -- even hardcoded returns, even obviously-incomplete logic. This is not laziness or naivete:\n\n- It **exposes refactoring opportunities** in the next phase. When the implementation does exactly one thing, structural smells are visible. Over-implemented green code looks \"already clean\" and hides design problems.\n- It **prevents premature generalization**. The shape of the right abstraction emerges from the second and third test, not the first. Implementing for hypothetical future tests locks in a design before its constraints are known.\n- It **keeps the red-green-refactor cycle short**. Each cycle pays a cost in tokens and context; over-implementing in green collapses several future cycles into one large one and loses the per-test feedback loop.\n\n## Your Mission\n\n1. Implement the **minimal code** necessary to make the failing test pass\n2. Use the **simplest possible solution** (hardcoded values are acceptable)\n3. Avoid adding features for future tests\n4. Verify all tests pass\n5. NO optimization, NO refactoring yet\n\n## Context: $ARGUMENTS\n\n## Green Phase Rules\n\n- **Minimal code only**: Just enough to pass the current test\n- **Baby steps**: Make the smallest possible change\n- **No future features**: Don't implement what future tests might need\n- **Simple is better**: Hardcoded returns are perfectly fine\n- **Tests must pass**: Verify all tests are green\n- **No refactoring yet**: Save improvements for Refactor phase\n\n## Process\n\n### Step 1: Analyze the Failing Test\n\nUnderstand what the test expects:\n- What input does the test provide?\n- What output does it expect?\n- What is the **simplest** way to produce that output?\n\n### Step 2: Write Minimal Implementation\n\nImplement **only what's needed** to make the current test pass:\n\n```typescript\n// For first test \"should return 0 for empty input\":\nexport const calculate = (input: string): number => {\n  return 0; // Minimal - just make the test pass\n};\n\n// For second test \"should return number for single input\":\nexport const calculate = (input: string): number => {\n  if (input === \"\") return 0;\n  return parseInt(input); // Still simple\n};\n\n// For third test \"should add two numbers\":\nexport const calculate = (input: string): number => {\n  if (input === \"\") return 0;\n  const numbers = input.split(\",\");\n  if (numbers.length === 1) return parseInt(numbers[0]);\n  return parseInt(numbers[0]) + parseInt(numbers[1]); // Only now add logic\n};\n```\n\n### Step 3: Run Tests\n\nRun `pnpm test` and verify:\n- Current test now passes\n- All previous tests still pass\n\n### Step 4: Verify No Over-Implementation\n\nCheck yourself:\n- Did I implement features for future tests? -> Remove them\n- Did I add logic not demanded by current test? -> Remove it\n- Did I optimize prematurely? -> Simplify\n- Did I refactor existing code? -> Revert, save for Refactor phase\n\n### Step 5: Report Completion\n\n```\nGreen Phase Complete:\n**Implementation**: [brief description of what was added]\n**Result**: All tests now pass ([X] passing)\n**Approach**: [explain why this is minimal]\n\nProceeding to Refactor phase.\n```\n\n## Minimal Implementation Strategies\n\n### Hardcoded Returns (Preferred for Early Tests)\n```typescript\n// Test: \"should return 0 for empty input\"\nreturn 0; // Perfect - minimal\n```\n\n### Simple Conditionals (When Multiple Tests)\n```typescript\n// Test: \"should return number for single input\"\nif (input === \"\") return 0;\nreturn parseInt(input); // Still simple\n```\n\n### Generalization (Only When Forced)\n```typescript\n// Test: \"should add multiple numbers\" - NOW generalize\nreturn input.split(\",\").reduce((sum, n) => sum + parseInt(n), 0);\n```\n\n## Important Guidelines\n\n### DO\n- Write minimal code to make test pass\n- Use hardcoded values when appropriate\n- Take baby steps\n- Verify all tests pass\n\n### DON'T\n- Implement beyond what tests demand\n- Add features for future tests\n- Optimize prematurely\n- Refactor during Green phase\n\n## Psychological Resistance\n\nYou will feel resistance:\n- **\"This is too simple\"** -> That's correct! Minimal is the way\n- **\"Hardcoded values feel wrong\"** -> They're exactly right for early tests\n- **\"I should implement ahead\"** -> Resist this strongly\n- **\"This is inefficient\"** -> Actually accelerates development\n\nTrust the process. Simple steps compound into elegant solutions.\n\n## Completion\n\nAfter completing Green phase, proceed to Refactor phase:\n\n```\nGreen Phase Complete. Proceeding to Refactor phase.\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944392999},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Green: implement high enchantment claim clause. Need to know enchantment level of damaged item. Damage entry has itemType, but not enchantment. We need to look up the policy item's enchantment. For each damage, find matching item in policy. Since policy items may have multiple of same type, for simplicity match first? But tests use one item. We'll need to handle counts later. Minimal: find first policy item with matching type and use its enchantment. For dragon material, use its material.\n\nImplement:\n```\nconst reimbursementForDamage = (policyItem, damage) => {\n  let amount = damage.amount;\n  if (policyItem.enchantment >= 8) amount *= 0.5;\n  // dragon material full reimbursement means no change\n  return Math.max(0, amount - 100);\n}\n```\n\nBut the spec order: high enchantment halves damage, then deductible. Dragon material full reimbursement means amount unchanged, then deductible. If both apply, high enchantment wins (50% then deductible). So check enchantment first, then deductible. Material doesn't change amount.\n\nWe need to pass policy items to processClaim and match damage to item. Minimal: match by type, assume one of each.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:175","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const processClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const cap = CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems(policyItems);\n  const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + Math.max(0, damage.amount - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE),\n    0\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(payoutBeforeCap, cap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: Math.floor(cap - payout) };\n};","newText":"const reimbursementForDamage = (policyItem: Item, damageAmount: number): number => {\n  const enchantment = typeof policyItem.enchantment === \"number\" ? policyItem.enchantment : 0;\n  const amountAfterClauses =\n    enchantment >= 8 ? damageAmount * 0.5 : damageAmount;\n  return Math.max(0, amountAfterClauses - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const cap = CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems(policyItems);\n  const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const policyItem = policyItems.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!policyItem) {\n      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} not insured`);\n    }\n    return sum + reimbursementForDamage(policyItem, damage.amount);\n  }, 0);\n  const payout = Math.min(payoutBeforeCap, cap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: Math.floor(cap - payout) };\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1147,"output":705,"cacheRead":120320,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":249,"totalTokens":122172,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944393005,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-201f7102-cf66-4db1-96bd-bd8e2e028f67","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:175","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 135     policyBase + calculatePolicyAdjustment(baseTotal, customerYears, isFollowUp) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n 136   return { premium: Math.ceil(rawPremium) };\n 137 };\n 138 \n+139 const reimbursementForDamage = (policyItem: Item, damageAmount: number): number => {\n+140   const enchantment = typeof policyItem.enchantment === \"number\" ? policyItem.enchantment : 0;\n+141   const amountAfterClauses =\n+142     enchantment >= 8 ? damageAmount * 0.5 : damageAmount;\n+143   return Math.max(0, amountAfterClauses - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n+144 };\n+145 \n 139 const processClaim = (\n 140   policyItems: Item[],\n 141   damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>\n 142 ): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n 143   const cap = CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems(policyItems);\n-144   const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce(\n-145     (sum, damage) => sum + Math.max(0, damage.amount - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE),\n-146     0\n-147   );\n+151   const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n+152     const policyItem = policyItems.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n+153     if (!policyItem) {\n+154       throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} not insured`);\n+155     }\n+156     return sum + reimbursementForDamage(policyItem, damage.amount);\n+157   }, 0);\n 148   const payout = Math.min(payoutBeforeCap, cap);\n 149   return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: Math.floor(cap - payout) };\n 150 };\n 151 \n     ...","patch":"--- src/claim-office.ts\n+++ src/claim-office.ts\n@@ -135,17 +135,27 @@\n     policyBase + calculatePolicyAdjustment(baseTotal, customerYears, isFollowUp) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n   return { premium: Math.ceil(rawPremium) };\n };\n \n+const reimbursementForDamage = (policyItem: Item, damageAmount: number): number => {\n+  const enchantment = typeof policyItem.enchantment === \"number\" ? policyItem.enchantment : 0;\n+  const amountAfterClauses =\n+    enchantment >= 8 ? damageAmount * 0.5 : damageAmount;\n+  return Math.max(0, amountAfterClauses - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n+};\n+\n const processClaim = (\n   policyItems: Item[],\n   damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>\n ): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n   const cap = CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems(policyItems);\n-  const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce(\n-    (sum, damage) => sum + Math.max(0, damage.amount - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE),\n-    0\n-  );\n+  const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n+    const policyItem = policyItems.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n+    if (!policyItem) {\n+      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} not insured`);\n+    }\n+    return sum + reimbursementForDamage(policyItem, damage.amount);\n+  }, 0);\n   const payout = Math.min(payoutBeforeCap, cap);\n   return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: Math.floor(cap - payout) };\n };\n \n","firstChangedLine":139},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944397345},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Run tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:176","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test 2>&1","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":90,"output":32,"cacheRead":122112,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4,"totalTokens":122234,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944397350,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0a9af994-dd0f-41ca-9f1c-02672d2907f9","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:176","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (39 tests | 12 skipped) 5ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  27 passed | 12 todo (39)\n   Start at  01:53:19\n   Duration  167ms (transform 35ms, setup 0ms, collect 33ms, tests 5ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944399255},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Green complete. Refactor.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Green -- Test 27: High-enchantment claim clause\n\nAdded per-damage reimbursement that halves damage when the insured item's enchantment is ≥ 8, then subtracts the deductible.\n\nGreen Phase Complete:\n**Implementation**: Looked up policy item by type and applied high-enchantment 50 % reduction before deductible\n**Result**: All tests pass (27 passing, 12 todo)\n**Approach**: Minimal claim special-clause handling\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.subagent:177","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 27\nRecent Green phase: Added per-damage reimbursement with high-enchantment halving before deductible.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","cwd":"."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":279,"output":218,"cacheRead":122176,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":122673,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944399262,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-fe12b474-dcb0-43a0-ac26-a2df3c93a1cb","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:177","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Summary\n\nAll 27 passing tests remain green after the refactoring.\n\n### Naming Evaluation (Rule 2 — first priority)\n\n| Name | Purpose | Assessment | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `valueForItem` | Returns the insured value of an item | Too generic; \"value\" could mean premium, market value, etc. | Rename to `insuredValueFor` |\n| `processStep` parameter `index` | Boolean flag indicating whether this step is a follow-up contract | Misleading — it's used only as `index > 0` | Rename parameter to `isFollowUp` |\n| `reimbursementForDamage` literals `8` and `0.5` | Business rule: high-enchantment damage threshold and halving rate | Magic numbers hide intent | Extract named constants |\n\n### Refactorings Applied\n\n1. **Renamed `valueForItem` → `insuredValueFor`**  \n   Better reveals that the value is the insured/replacement value used for caps, not the premium.\n\n2. **Renamed `processStep` parameter `index` → `isFollowUp`**  \n   The parameter was always treated as a boolean (`index > 0`). The new name makes the contract explicit.\n\n3. **Extracted high-enchantment damage constants**  \n   Added `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8` and `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE = 0.5` to replace magic numbers in `reimbursementForDamage`.\n\n### Duplication Check (Rule 3)\n\n- Minor structural similarity between `BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword` and `INSURANCE_VALUES[type] ?? INSURANCE_VALUES.sword` was left as-is; extracting a generic fallback helper would add abstraction without improving clarity.\n- The `typeof item.enchantment === \"number\"` guard appears twice but with different thresholds and semantics; a shared helper would add more elements than it removes.\n\n### APP Mass Calculation\n\nMass counted on the changed regions:\n\n**`reimbursementForDamage` before:**\n```ts\nconst amountAfterClauses =\n  enchantment >= 8 ? damageAmount * 0.5 : damageAmount;\n```\n- Constants: `0`, `0`, `0.5`, `8` → 4\n- Bindings: `policyItem`, `damageAmount`, `enchantment`, `amountAfterClauses` → 4\n- Invocations: `*`, `Math.max`, `-` → 3\n- Conditionals: `?:` × 2 → 2\n- **Mass: 22**\n\n**`reimbursementForDamage` after:**\n```ts\nconst amountAfterClauses =\n  enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD\n    ? damageAmount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE\n    : damageAmount;\n```\n- Constants: `0`, `0` → 2\n- Bindings: same 4\n- Invocations: same 3\n- Conditionals: same 2\n- **Mass: 20**\n\n**New top-level constants:**\n- `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8` → 1 binding + 1 constant = 2\n- `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE = 0.5` → 1 binding + 1 constant = 2\n- **Mass: 4**\n\n**Net mass change:** `22 → 24` for this concern (**+2 mass**).\n\n**`processStep` / `processScenario` rename:** no mass change (the `index > 0` comparison moved from callee to caller).\n\n### Why Mass Increased\n\nThe mass increased by 2 because two magic numbers were promoted to named constants. This is a deliberate Rule-2 trade-off: **clarity trumps lower mass**. The constants now document that the damage threshold (8) and reduction rate (0.5) are distinct from the quote surcharge threshold (5) and rate (0.3).\n\n### Final Verification\n\n- `pnpm test`: **27 passed | 12 todo**\n- `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`: **no errors**\n\nRefactoring complete."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 27\nRecent Green phase: Added per-damage reimbursement with high-enchantment halving before deductible.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 27\nRecent Green phase: Added per-damage reimbursement with high-enchantment halving before deductible.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784944403739},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the implementation file and test file to understand the current code.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":85,"output":56,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":18,"totalTokens":6157,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944403758,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ce62c400-a71c-4ee8-b790-921b8d4ed99b","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n  damage?: number;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: {\n    cause: string;\n    damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>;\n  };\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\";\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (type: string): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n\nconst basePremiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  isComponent(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * basePremiumForItem(type);\n\nconst surchargeWhen = (applies: boolean, base: number, rate: number): number =>\n  applies ? base * rate : 0;\n\nconst surchargeForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item.type);\n  return (\n    surchargeWhen(item.cursed ?? false, base, CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE) +\n    surchargeWhen(\n      typeof item.enchantment === \"number\" && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n      base,\n      HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    )\n  );\n};\n\nconst valueForItem = (type: string): number =>\n  INSURANCE_VALUES[type] ?? INSURANCE_VALUES.sword;\n\nconst insuranceSumForItems = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + valueForItem(item.type), 0);\n\nconst basePremiumTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const quantityByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    quantityByType.set(item.type, (quantityByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  });\n\n  return Array.from(quantityByType.entries()).reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + basePremiumForGroup(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n};\n\nconst calculatePolicyAdjustment = (\n  baseTotal: number,\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customerYears >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD\n      ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE * baseTotal\n      : 0;\n\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE * baseTotal;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFollowUp ? FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE * baseTotal : 0;\n\n  return -loyaltyDiscount + firstInsuranceSurcharge - followUpDiscount;\n};\n\nconst quoteForItems = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): { premium: number } => {\n  const baseTotal = basePremiumTotal(items);\n\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce(\n    (total, item) => total + surchargeForItem(item),\n    0\n  );\n\n  const policyBase = baseTotal + itemSurcharges;\n  const rawPremium =\n    policyBase + calculatePolicyAdjustment(baseTotal, customerYears, isFollowUp) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(rawPremium) };\n};\n\nconst reimbursementForDamage = (policyItem: Item, damageAmount: number): number => {\n  const enchantment = typeof policyItem.enchantment === \"number\" ? policyItem.enchantment : 0;\n  const amountAfterClauses =\n    enchantment >= 8 ? damageAmount * 0.5 : damageAmount;\n  return Math.max(0, amountAfterClauses - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const cap = CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems(policyItems);\n  const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const policyItem = policyItems.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!policyItem) {\n      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} not insured`);\n    }\n    return sum + reimbursementForDamage(policyItem, damage.amount);\n  }, 0);\n  const payout = Math.min(payoutBeforeCap, cap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: Math.floor(cap - payout) };\n};\n\nconst processStep = (\n  scenario: Scenario,\n  step: Step,\n  index: number\n): { premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n    return quoteForItems(step.items, scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, index > 0);\n  }\n  const policyStep = scenario.steps[step.policy] as QuoteStep;\n  return processClaim(policyStep.items, step.incident.damages);\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> =>\n  scenario.steps.map((step, index) => processStep(scenario, step, index));\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944404812},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quote premiums\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"oak\", enchantment: 1, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 93 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 49 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single moonstone -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Component block rules\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes without block discount -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 60 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote exactly 3 runes with block discount -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 198 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not mix different component types for the block discount -- 2 runes + 1 moonstone premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 88 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply separate blocks for each component type -- 3 runes + 3 moonstones premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 137 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should add cursed surcharge to a sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 165 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at level 5 -- premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges -- premium 195 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 195 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge below level 5 -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply first insurance surcharge -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on the second quote -- premium 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }, { premium: 100 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply item-specific modifiers per item and policy-wide modifiers on policy base -- cursed sword + plain amulet premium 231 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n            { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 231 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it(\"should compute newcomer with a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 165 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should compute long-standing customer's second contract -- premium 160 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }, { premium: 160 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Claim standard reimbursement\n  it(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G, remaining cap 1600 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should reimburse a rune damage minus deductible -- payout 100 G, remaining cap 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }, { payout: 100, remainingCap: 400 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Claim special clauses\n  it(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage minus deductible -- payout 700 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 700, remainingCap: 1300 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should halve damage for enchantment level 9 or higher -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"magic surge\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }]);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should apply enchantment clause over dragon material when both apply -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply dragon-material clause when only it applies -- payout 700 G\");\n\n  // Multi-item / deductible\n  it.todo(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident -- total payout 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should sum insurance values for multiple items of the same type -- cap 4000 G\");\n\n  // Cap exhaustion\n  it.todo(\"should cap the first claim and track remaining cap -- first payout 1400 G, remaining 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should reduce the second claim by remaining cap -- second payout 600 G, remaining 0 G\");\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 7 runes with first insurance yields 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- high-enchantment damage 901 G yields 350 G\");\n\n  // Error cases\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in quote\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in claim\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject negative damage amount\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject more damages than insured items\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944404812},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me run the tests first to make sure they pass.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":4846,"output":37,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":13,"totalTokens":11027,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944404812,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-57c202c0-3630-4e07-86b7-26ab53af47d4","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experim