ount`, matching the domain concept (surcharge minus discounts).\n3. **Type safety / intent**: Extracted `quoteStepForPolicy` to replace the unsafe `as QuoteStep` cast with an explicit, named lookup that also guards against a claim step being used as a policy.\n4. **Clarity**: Extracted `capForPolicy` so `processScenario` reads as `const cap = capForPolicy(policyStep.items)` instead of an inline multiplication.\n\n## Duplication Evaluation\n\n- `basePremiumForItem` and `insuredValueFor` are structurally similar lookups, but a generic `valueForType(table, type)` helper would obscure the domain meaning of *base premium* vs. *insured value*. Left them separate per Rule 2.\n- `surchargeWhen` already removes duplication between cursed and high-enchantment surcharges; kept as-is.\n\n## Tests\n\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  33 passed | 6 todo (39)\n```\n\nAll 33 passing tests stay green; the 6 `it.todo` tests remain untouched."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 33\nRecent Green phase: Added per-policy remaining cap tracking across claim steps.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 33\nRecent Green phase: Added per-policy remaining cap tracking across claim steps.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784944515237},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by understanding the codebase. I need to read the test file and implementation file, then run tests to ensure they pass, and then refactor while keeping tests green.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the test file, implementation file, and running the tests to establish a baseline."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":80,"output":115,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":36,"totalTokens":6211,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944515260,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-39b36ff0-ce54-4f58-87d6-e4dd31e1a5ab","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quote premiums\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"oak\", enchantment: 1, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 93 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 49 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single moonstone -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Component block rules\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes without block discount -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 60 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote exactly 3 runes with block discount -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 198 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not mix different component types for the block discount -- 2 runes + 1 moonstone premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 88 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply separate blocks for each component type -- 3 runes + 3 moonstones premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 137 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should add cursed surcharge to a sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 165 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at level 5 -- premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges -- premium 195 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 195 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge below level 5 -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply first insurance surcharge -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on the second quote -- premium 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }, { premium: 100 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply item-specific modifiers per item and policy-wide modifiers on policy base -- cursed sword + plain amulet premium 231 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n            { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 231 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it(\"should compute newcomer with a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 165 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should compute long-standing customer's second contract -- premium 160 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }, { premium: 160 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Claim standard reimbursement\n  it(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G, remaining cap 1600 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should reimburse a rune damage minus deductible -- payout 100 G, remaining cap 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }, { payout: 100, remainingCap: 400 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Claim special clauses\n  it(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage minus deductible -- payout 700 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 700, remainingCap: 1300 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should halve damage for enchantment level 9 or higher -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"magic surge\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply enchantment clause over dragon material when both apply -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply dragon-material clause when only it applies -- payout 700 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 700, remainingCap: 1300 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Multi-item / deductible\n  it(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident -- total payout 600 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false },\n            { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [\n              { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n              { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 },\n            ],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([\n      { premium: 181 },\n      { payout: 600, remainingCap: 2600 },\n    ]);\n  });\n  it(\"should sum insurance values for multiple items of the same type -- cap 4000 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false },\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 100 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 225 }, { payout: 0, remainingCap: 4000 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Cap exhaustion\n  it(\"should cap the first claim and track remaining cap -- first payout 1400 G, remaining 600 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 1400, remainingCap: 600 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should reduce the second claim by remaining cap -- second payout 600 G, remaining 0 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }],\n          },\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([\n      { premium: 115 },\n      { payout: 1400, remainingCap: 600 },\n      { payout: 600, remainingCap: 0 },\n    ]);\n  });\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 7 runes with first insurance yields 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- high-enchantment damage 901 G yields 350 G\");\n\n  // Error cases\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in quote\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in claim\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject negative damage amount\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject more damages than insured items\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944516769},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n  damage?: number;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: {\n    cause: string;\n    damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>;\n  };\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\";\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (type: string): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n\nconst basePremiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  isComponent(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * basePremiumForItem(type);\n\nconst surchargeWhen = (applies: boolean, base: number, rate: number): number =>\n  applies ? base * rate : 0;\n\nconst surchargeForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item.type);\n  return (\n    surchargeWhen(item.cursed ?? false, base, CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE) +\n    surchargeWhen(\n      typeof item.enchantment === \"number\" && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n      base,\n      HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    )\n  );\n};\n\nconst insuredValueFor = (type: string): number =>\n  INSURANCE_VALUES[type] ?? INSURANCE_VALUES.sword;\n\nconst insuranceSumForItems = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuredValueFor(item.type), 0);\n\nconst basePremiumTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const quantityByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    quantityByType.set(item.type, (quantityByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  });\n\n  return Array.from(quantityByType.entries()).reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + basePremiumForGroup(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n};\n\nconst calculatePolicyAdjustment = (\n  baseTotal: number,\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customerYears >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD\n      ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE * baseTotal\n      : 0;\n\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE * baseTotal;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFollowUp ? FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE * baseTotal : 0;\n\n  return -loyaltyDiscount + firstInsuranceSurcharge - followUpDiscount;\n};\n\nconst quoteForItems = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): { premium: number } => {\n  const baseTotal = basePremiumTotal(items);\n\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce(\n    (total, item) => total + surchargeForItem(item),\n    0\n  );\n\n  const policyBase = baseTotal + itemSurcharges;\n  const rawPremium =\n    policyBase + calculatePolicyAdjustment(baseTotal, customerYears, isFollowUp) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(rawPremium) };\n};\n\nconst reimbursementForDamage = (policyItem: Item, damageAmount: number): number => {\n  const enchantment = typeof policyItem.enchantment === \"number\" ? policyItem.enchantment : 0;\n  const amountAfterClauses =\n    enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD\n      ? damageAmount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE\n      : damageAmount;\n  return Math.max(0, amountAfterClauses - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>,\n  remainingCap: number\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const policyItem = policyItems.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!policyItem) {\n      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} not insured`);\n    }\n    return sum + reimbursementForDamage(policyItem, damage.amount);\n  }, 0);\n  const payout = Math.min(payoutBeforeCap, remainingCap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: Math.floor(remainingCap - payout) };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> => {\n  const remainingCapByPolicy = new Map<number, number>();\n  return scenario.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      return quoteForItems(step.items, scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, index > 0);\n    }\n    const policyStep = scenario.steps[step.policy] as QuoteStep;\n    const cap = CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems(policyStep.items);\n    const remainingCap = remainingCapByPolicy.get(step.policy) ?? cap;\n    const result = processClaim(policyStep.items, step.incident.damages, remainingCap);\n    remainingCapByPolicy.set(step.policy, result.remainingCap);\n    return result;\n  });\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944516769},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (39 tests | 6 skipped) 9ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  33 passed | 6 todo (39)\n   Start at  01:55:16\n   Duration  182ms (transform 38ms, setup 0ms, collect 49ms, tests 9ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944516769},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Tests are green (33 passing, 6 todo). Now I need to refactor the implementation.\n\nLet me first perform naming evaluation, then calculate APP mass, then apply Simple Design Rules.\n\n### Naming Evaluation\n\nCurrent function names:\n- `processScenario` - processes a scenario of quote/claim steps. Seems reasonable.\n- `isComponent` - checks if a type is a component (rune/moonstone). Reasonable.\n- `basePremiumForItem` - gets base premium for an item type. Reasonable.\n- `basePremiumForGroup` - gets base premium for a group of items of same type. Reasonable.\n- `surchargeWhen` - calculates surcharge when condition applies. OK.\n- `surchargeForItem` - calculates surcharge for an item. Reasonable.\n- `insuredValueFor` - gets insurance value for type. Reasonable.\n- `insuranceSumForItems` - sums insurance values for items. Reasonable.\n- `basePremiumTotal` - total base premium for items. Reasonable.\n- `calculatePolicyAdjustment` - calculates policy adjustment. OK, but \"adjustment\" is a bit generic. It handles loyalty, first insurance, follow-up. Maybe `policyDiscountsAndSurcharges`? Hmm.\n- `quoteForItems` - creates quote for items. Reasonable.\n- `reimbursementForDamage` - calculates reimbursement for a damage. Reasonable.\n- `processClaim` - processes a claim. Reasonable.\n\nPotential issues:\n1. `calculatePolicyAdjustment` is a bit generic. But maybe acceptable.\n2. `reimbursementForDamage` takes a `policyItem` and `damageAmount`. The name is OK.\n3. `processScenario` does multiple things (quotes and claims), but the domain name fits.\n\n### APP Mass Calculation\n\nLet me count the mass of the current implementation file `src/claim-office.ts`.\n\nConstants (Mass 1): 14\n- PROCESSING_FEE = 5\n- COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3\n- COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60\n- CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5\n- HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3\n- HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5\n- HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8\n- HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE = 0.5\n- LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2\n- LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2\n- FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1\n- FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15\n- DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100\n- CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2\n\nLiteral values in code:\n- BASE_PREMIUMS object keys (not values? Actually constants are literal values. Keys are bindings? Hmm.)\nActually constants = literal values. So in `BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {...}` there are 6 number literals. In `INSURANCE_VALUES` there are 6 number literals.\n- string literals? `sword`, `amulet`, `staff`, etc. - these are constant string literals. But they're used as keys. Should I count them? The APP definition says \"Literal values (`5`, `\"hello\"`, `true`)\". So yes, string literals count too.\n\nWait, but that could inflate mass significantly. Let me focus on the actual code logic, not data tables. The mass calculation should be on the implementation logic, not necessarily static data. But the rules say count constants.\n\nLet me count carefully for the entire file.\n\nActually, this is getting complex. Let me count mass for the dynamic functions primarily.\n\nFunctions:\n1. `isComponent` - 1 conditional (||), 2 string literals (\"rune\", \"moonstone\"), 1 param.\n   Mass: constants 2, bindings 1, conditionals 4 = 7\n\n2. `basePremiumForItem` - 1 param, 1 conditional (??), 1 constant (BASE_PREMIUMS.sword string), 1 invocation/property access.\n   Mass: bindings 1, constants 1, conditionals 4 = 6\n\n3. `basePremiumForGroup` - 2 params, 1 conditional (&& and ===), 1 invocation, 1 constant (COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE).\n   Mass: bindings 2, constants 1, invocations 2, conditionals 4 = 9\n\n4. `surchargeWhen` - 3 params, 1 conditional (?:).\n   Mass: bindings 3, conditionals 4 = 7\n\n5. `surchargeForItem` - 1 param, 1 const base, 2 invocations, 2 conditionals (?? and >=), 2 constants (HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD number).\n   Actually `item.cursed ?? false` is conditional. `item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD` is conditional. The surchargeWhen calls are invocations.\n   Mass: bindings 2 (item, base), constants 1 (HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD - but it's a binding reference, not literal), invocations 3, conditionals 8 = 14\n   Wait, `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD` is a binding reference. Constants count only literal values. So no constant there.\n\n6. `insuredValueFor` - similar to basePremiumForItem. Mass ~6\n\n7. `insuranceSumForItems` - 1 param, 1 reduce (loop), 2 bindings in callback, 1 invocation.\n   Mass: bindings 3, invocations 2, loops 5 = 10\n\n8. `basePremiumTotal` - 1 param, 1 const quantityByType, 1 forEach (loop), 2 assignments, 1 reduce (loop).\n   Mass: bindings 5, invocations 3, loops 10, assignments 12 = 30\n\n9. `calculatePolicyAdjustment` - 3 params, 3 consts, 3 conditionals (>=, * is not conditional, the ?: for followUp).\n   Actually `customerYears >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? ... : ...` is 1 conditional. `isFollowUp ? ... : ...` is 1 conditional. Total 2 conditionals.\n   Invocations: 3 multiplications? Multiplication is not an invocation. Return expression has additions/subtractions.\n   Mass: bindings 6, conditionals 8 = 14\n\n10. `quoteForItems` - 3 params, 3 consts, 1 reduce (loop), 2 invocations (calculatePolicyAdjustment), 1 conditional in map (index > 0).\n    Mass: bindings 7, invocations 4, loops 5, conditionals 4 = 20\n\n11. `reimbursementForDamage` - 2 params, 1 const enchantment, 1 conditional (?: with >=), 1 invocation (Math.max), 1 subtraction.\n    Mass: bindings 4, invocations 2, conditionals 4 = 10\n\n12. `processClaim` - 3 params, 1 const payoutBeforeCap, 1 reduce (loop), 2 conditionals (find and if), 1 invocation (Math.min), 2 assignments in return.\n    Mass: bindings 6, invocations 4, loops 5, conditionals 8, assignments 12 = 35\n\n13. `processScenario` - 1 param, 1 const remainingCapByPolicy, 1 map (loop), 1 conditional (if step.op === \"quote\"), several property accesses and invocations.\n    Mass: bindings 6, invocations 6, loops 5, conditionals 4, assignments 6 = 27\n\nTotal mass (rough): 7+6+9+7+14+6+10+30+14+20+10+35+27 = 185\n\nThis is a rough estimate. But I should be more careful.\n\nLet me think about what refactorings would actually improve the code.\n\n### Identifying Refactoring Opportunities\n\nLooking at the code, I see several issues:\n\n1. **Naming/Clarity in `processScenario`**: The variable `policyStep` is used both as the quote step for the policy and for its items. The naming is OK but could be clearer.\n\n2. **Duplication/Conceptual duplication in constants**: The constants `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD` and `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD` are related to enchantment. OK.\n\n3. **`basePremiumForItem` and `insuredValueFor` duplication**: These two functions are nearly identical in structure - they both look up a value by type with a fallback to sword.\n   ```typescript\n   const basePremiumForItem = (type: string): number =>\n     BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? BASE_PREMIUMS.sword;\n   \n   const insuredValueFor = (type: string): number =>\n     INSURANCE_VALUES[type] ?? INSURANCE_VALUES.sword;\n   ```\n   This is clear duplication. We could extract a generic lookup function.\n\n4. **`processClaim` error handling**: It throws for unknown item type in claim, but the test has this as `it.todo`, so maybe not tested yet. But existing code has it.\n\n5. **`calculatePolicyAdjustment`**: The formula `-loyaltyDiscount + firstInsuranceSurcharge - followUpDiscount` is a bit cryptic. Could be clearer.\n\n6. **`processScenario` cap tracking**: It's doing per-policy remaining cap tracking. The recent change was \"Added per-policy remaining cap tracking across claim steps.\" Maybe we can make this clearer.\n\n7. **Type safety**: The cast `scenario.steps[step.policy] as QuoteStep` is a bit unsafe. Could improve with a helper.\n\nLet me look for the most impactful refactoring that keeps tests green.\n\n### Refactoring Plan\n\nI'll focus on:\n1. Extract a generic `lookupWithFallback` to remove duplication between `basePremiumForItem` and `insuredValueFor`.\n2. Maybe rename `calculatePolicyAdjustment` to something clearer like `policyModifierAmount`.\n3. Improve `processScenario` with better naming and perhaps a helper for policy lookup.\n\nLet me start with the duplication removal since that's a clear Rule 3 win.\n\nBut first, I should evaluate naming more carefully.\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- `basePremiumForItem` vs `insuredValueFor`: both are lookups. Could have more consistent naming, but they're descriptive.\n- `calculatePolicyAdjustment`: This calculates the net adjustment from discounts/surcharges. A better name might be `policyModifierTotal` or `loyaltyAndContractAdjustment`. The current name is somewhat vague but acceptable.\n- `