arefully to avoid errors.\n\nLet's recalc with a consistent methodology.\n\nMass components:\n- Constant: numeric/string/boolean/undefined literals. We'll list them.\n- Binding: parameters and local const variables (bindings). Declared const are bindings. In arrow function expression, the function name is a binding constant; do we count it? The function identifier itself is a binding. For each function declaration `const foo = (...)`, `foo` is a binding. In APP sample they counted variables and parameters, not function names? They counted `numbers, sum, num` not `calculate`. We'll not count top-level const function names to avoid inflation. But we could include; consistency matters. We didn't count function names. Good.\n\n- Invocation: function/method/constructor calls. Count each call.\n\n- Conditional: `if`, ternary `?:`. Should we count `??`? In our mass, we counted `??` as conditional for surchargeForItem. But after refactor it's still there. Since delta unaffected, fine. But if we want rigorous, maybe don't count `??` because not in list. Let's decide: We'll count `if` and `?:` only. Then surchargeForItem mass changes? Original surchargeForItem: constants false, \"number\" =2; bindings item,base=2; invocations 3; conditionals 0 (no if/ternary). Total=7. After same 7. policyAdjustment: 18. basePremiumForItem:8. insuredValueFor:8. surchargeWhen:8. Sum before=8+8+7+8+18+8 (basePremiumForGroup? we included group before 8) =57? Let's recompute region with no `??` count:\nbasePremiumForItem 8\nbasePremiumForGroup 8\nsurchargeWhen 8\nsurchargeForItem 7\ninsuredValueFor 8\npolicyAdjustment 18\nSum =57.\nAfter:\nlookupValue 9\nbasePremiumForItem 2\nbasePremiumForGroup 8\nconditionalAdjustment 8\nsurchargeForItem 7\ninsuredValueFor 2\npolicyAdjustment 18\nSum=54. Delta -3. Same delta. Good. So counting `??` doesn't change delta. We'll present counts maybe include `??` or not; but explain methodology.\n\nLet's verify lookupValue mass: bindings table,type,value=3; constants undefined=1, template string=1; invocations throw new Error=1; conditional if=1. Total 9. Yes.\n\nbasePremiumForItem after: bindings type=1; invocations lookupValue=1; total 2.\ninsuredValueFor after: 2.\nconditionalAdjustment after: bindings applies,base,rate=3; constant 0=1; conditional ternary=1; total 8.\npolicyAdjustment after: same as before: bindings 6; invocations conditionalAdjustment x2 =4; conditionals ternary x2 =8; total 18.\n\nSo region delta -3. Good.\n\nBut is the `conditionalAdjustment` function name change itself a mass change? No.\n\nNow maybe we can attempt another refactor to reduce mass more: combine lookup helper usage with constants? Not needed.\n\nHowever, note that `basePremiumForItem` now has only `lookupValue` invocation, no conditional. That means if unknown type in quote, error thrown from helper. Good. `insuredValueFor` same.\n\nPotential issue: The helper uses generic error message \"Unknown item type\" without specifying table. Tests only check `toThrow()` for quote unknown item. Claim unknown item is still todo. Should be okay.\n\nNow final response. Need include report. The user asked \"Run autonomously, return when done.\" As subagent, final should summarize. The main harness expects the subagent to return. We can output markdown summary. Include:\n- Refactoring applied\n- Naming evaluation\n- Mass before/after\n- Tests status\n\nLet's write final answer. Need not write experiment-done.txt (that's main agent's job). Just return summary.\n\nBefore final, maybe run pnpm test once more to be safe. Already run after edit. But okay.\n\nLet's also maybe check `pnpm test -- --reporter=verbose`? Not needed.\n\nNeed include file path. We changed src/claim-office.ts.\n\nOne concern: The APP mass calculation should be transparent. We'll show a table.\n\nLet's craft final response with sections:\n- Naming Evaluation\n- Current Code Mass (affected functions)\n- Refactoring Applied\n- New Code Mass\n- Tests\n- Decision\n\nLet's ensure we mention all tests green: 36 passing, 3 skipped (todos).\n\nPotential need to mention Rule priorities: Rule 2 rename, Rule 3 lookup helper, Rule 4 mass lower.\n\nLet's produce final.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring complete.\n\n## Naming Evaluation\n\n| Name | Purpose | Assessment | Decision |\n|------|---------|------------|----------|\n| `surchargeWhen` | Returns `base * rate` when a condition is true | Misleading: it is also used for **discounts** (`loyaltyDiscount`, `followUpDiscount`) | Rename to `conditionalAdjustment` |\n| `basePremiumForItem` / `insuredValueFor` | Look up a value in a table and throw on unknown types | Duplicated `if (value === undefined) { throw ... }` pattern | Extract shared helper `lookupValue` |\n| Other names (`processScenario`, `processClaim`, `quoteForItems`, etc.) | Match their behaviour | Clear enough | Keep |\n\n## APP Mass — Affected Code\n\nCounted on the changed functions only (`basePremiumForItem`, `insuredValueFor`, `lookupValue`, `conditionalAdjustment`, `surchargeForItem`, `policyAdjustmentAmount`, `basePremiumForGroup`).\n\n### Before\n\n```\nbasePremiumForItem        : bindings 2 + constants 1 + invocation 1 + conditional 1  =  8\nbasePremiumForGroup       : bindings 2 + invocations 2 + conditional 1             =  8\nsurchargeWhen             : bindings 3 + constants 1 + conditional 1                 =  8\nsurchargeForItem          : bindings 2 + constants 2 + invocations 3               =  7\ninsuredValueFor           : bindings 2 + constants 1 + invocation 1 + conditional 1  =  8\npolicyAdjustmentAmount    : bindings 6 + invocations 2 + conditionals 2              = 18\n```\n\n**Total mass before: 57**\n\n### After\n\n```\nlookupValue               : bindings 3 + constants 1 + invocation 1 + conditional 1  =  9\nbasePremiumForItem        : binding 1 + invocation 1                                =  2\nbasePremiumForGroup       : bindings 2 + invocations 2 + conditional 1                  =  8\nconditionalAdjustment     : bindings 3 + constants 1 + conditional 1                  =  8\nsurchargeForItem          : bindings 2 + constants 2 + invocations 3                  =  7\ninsuredValueFor           : binding 1 + invocation 1                                  =  2\npolicyAdjustmentAmount    : bindings 6 + invocations 2 + conditionals 2               = 18\n```\n\n**Total mass after: 54**\n\n**Mass change: 57 → 54 (−3)**\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\nIn `src/claim-office.ts`:\n\n1. **Renamed `surchargeWhen` → `conditionalAdjustment`**  \n   - The function is used for surcharges *and* discounts, so the old name was hiding intent.\n\n2. **Extracted `lookupValue` helper**  \n   - `basePremiumForItem` and `insuredValueFor` had identical `undefined`-check-and-throw logic.\n   - Now both delegate to `lookupValue(table, type)`, eliminating the duplication and keeping the error behaviour identical.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\npnpm test\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```\n✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (39 tests | 3 skipped) 7ms\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  36 passed | 3 todo (39)\n```\n\nAll existing tests stay green; the three `it.todo` tests remain as placeholders."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1825,"output":6069,"cacheRead":19136,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5334,"totalTokens":27030,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784944672888,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-94ccb5b8-9de7-44d5-8b6a-e40b3612687b","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":8506,"output":12587,"cacheRead":50368,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":27030,"turns":4},"model":"requesty/tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944699713},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Check file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:216","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":768,"output":24,"cacheRead":143424,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4,"totalTokens":144216,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944699720,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3feedb44-81e1-475e-b427-d7a54f030f45","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:216","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n  damage?: number;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: {\n    cause: string;\n    damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>;\n  };\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\";\n\nconst lookupValue = (table: Record<string, number>, type: string): number => {\n  const value = table[type];\n  if (value === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n  }\n  return value;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (type: string): number => lookupValue(BASE_PREMIUMS, type);\n\nconst basePremiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  isComponent(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * basePremiumForItem(type);\n\nconst conditionalAdjustment = (applies: boolean, base: number, rate: number): number =>\n  applies ? base * rate : 0;\n\nconst surchargeForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item.type);\n  return (\n    conditionalAdjustment(item.cursed ?? false, base, CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE) +\n    conditionalAdjustment(\n      typeof item.enchantment === \"number\" && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n      base,\n      HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    )\n  );\n};\n\nconst insuredValueFor = (type: string): number => lookupValue(INSURANCE_VALUES, type);\n\nconst insuranceSumForItems = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuredValueFor(item.type), 0);\n\nconst basePremiumTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const quantityByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    quantityByType.set(item.type, (quantityByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  });\n\n  return Array.from(quantityByType.entries()).reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + basePremiumForGroup(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n};\n\nconst policyAdjustmentAmount = (\n  baseTotal: number,\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount = conditionalAdjustment(\n    customerYears >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD,\n    baseTotal,\n    LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE * baseTotal;\n  const followUpDiscount = conditionalAdjustment(\n    isFollowUp,\n    baseTotal,\n    FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE\n  );\n\n  return firstInsuranceSurcharge - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n};\n\nconst quoteForItems = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): { premium: number } => {\n  const baseTotal = basePremiumTotal(items);\n\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce(\n    (total, item) => total + surchargeForItem(item),\n    0\n  );\n\n  const policyBase = baseTotal + itemSurcharges;\n  const rawPremium =\n    policyBase + policyAdjustmentAmount(baseTotal, customerYears, isFollowUp) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(rawPremium) };\n};\n\nconst reimbursementForDamage = (policyItem: Item, damageAmount: number): number => {\n  const enchantment = typeof policyItem.enchantment === \"number\" ? policyItem.enchantment : 0;\n  const damageAfterEnchantmentReduction =\n    enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD\n      ? damageAmount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE\n      : damageAmount;\n  return Math.max(0, damageAfterEnchantmentReduction - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst capForPolicy = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems(items);\n\nconst quoteStepForPolicy = (steps: Step[], policyIndex: number): QuoteStep => {\n  const step = steps[policyIndex];\n  if (step.op !== \"quote\") {\n    throw new Error(`Policy ${policyIndex} is not a quote step`);\n  }\n  return step;\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>,\n  remainingCap: number\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const policyItem = policyItems.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!policyItem) {\n      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} not insured`);\n    }\n    return sum + reimbursementForDamage(policyItem, damage.amount);\n  }, 0);\n  const payout = Math.floor(Math.min(payoutBeforeCap, remainingCap));\n  return { payout, remainingCap: Math.floor(remainingCap - payout) };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> => {\n  const remainingCapByPolicy = new Map<number, number>();\n  return scenario.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFollowUp = index > 0;\n      return quoteForItems(step.items, scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFollowUp);\n    }\n    const policyStep = quoteStepForPolicy(scenario.steps, step.policy);\n    const cap = capForPolicy(policyStep.items);\n    const remainingCap = remainingCapByPolicy.get(step.policy) ?? cap;\n    const result = processClaim(policyStep.items, step.incident.damages, remainingCap);\n    remainingCapByPolicy.set(step.policy, result.remainingCap);\n    return result;\n  });\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944701409},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Run tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:217","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test 2>&1","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1631,"output":32,"cacheRead":144192,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4,"totalTokens":145855,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944701412,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-f86305cb-754d-4015-becc-b581067ebef0","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:217","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (3