:189,"cacheRead":148864,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":149293,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944721098,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b4dc9f89-1482-454f-bdbc-6d56f471fe12","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:225","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Refactoring Complete**\n\n### Naming Evaluation\n- `conditionalAdjustment` → `rateAdjustmentIf`: The helper applies a rate-based adjustment only when a condition is true. The new name reveals that intent more directly.\n- `quoteStepForPolicy` → `requireQuoteStepAt`: The function validates that the step exists and is a quote, throwing otherwise. `require` captures the guard/validation nature.\n- `processClaim`: Name still fits — it settles a single claim and returns payout and remaining cap.\n- `reimbursementForDamage`: Name fits the pure damage calculation; extracted validation/lookup sibling is `reimbursementForDamageEntry`.\n\n### Refactorings Applied\n1. **Extracted `sum` helper** and replaced three `reduce(..., 0)` summations (`insuranceSumForItems`, item surcharges in `quoteForItems`, and group premium total in `basePremiumTotal`). This removes conceptual duplication and makes the summing intent explicit.\n2. **Renamed `conditionalAdjustment` → `rateAdjustmentIf`** and `quoteStepForPolicy` → `requireQuoteStepAt`** to better reveal intent.\n3. **Extracted `reimbursementForDamageEntry`** from `processClaim`, isolating per-damage validation and policy-item lookup from cap/payout arithmetic.\n4. **Removed unused `damage?: number` field** from the `Item` interface (fewest elements).\n\n### APP Mass (affected functions)\n**Before:** 105  \n**After:** 99  \n**Change:** -6\n\nBreakdown:\n| Area | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `insuranceSumForItems` | 13 | 6 |\n| `quoteForItems` surcharges | 14 | 6 |\n| `basePremiumTotal` group reduce | 15 | 8 |\n| `processClaim` | 45 | 21 |\n| `reimbursementForDamageEntry` (new) | — | 26 |\n| `sum` helper (new) | — | 14 |\n| `rateAdjustmentIf` / `requireQuoteStepAt` | 18 | 18 |\n\n### Tests\n- `pnpm test`: **38 passed, 1 todo**\n- `pnpm tsc --noEmit`: **no errors**"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 38\nRecent Green phase: Added negative damage amount validation in processClaim.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 38\nRecent Green phase: Added negative damage amount validation in processClaim.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. The project uses TypeScript and Vitest; run `pnpm test` to verify.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784944723823},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by understanding the task. I need to refactor the implementation in src/claim-office.ts while keeping all 38 tests passing. The recent green phase added negative damage amount validation in processClaim.\n\nI should:\n1. Read the implementation file and test file\n2. Evaluate naming first\n3. Calculate APP mass before\n4. Apply simple design rules\n5. Run tests after each change\n6. Calculate APP mass after\n7. Document decisions\n\nLet me start by reading the files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":79,"output":141,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":103,"totalTokens":6236,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944723851,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8bfeab68-adb8-475d-a0c7-927a6866630d","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n  damage?: number;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: {\n    cause: string;\n    damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>;\n  };\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\";\n\nconst lookupValue = (table: Record<string, number>, type: string): number => {\n  const value = table[type];\n  if (value === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n  }\n  return value;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (type: string): number => lookupValue(BASE_PREMIUMS, type);\n\nconst basePremiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  isComponent(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * basePremiumForItem(type);\n\nconst conditionalAdjustment = (applies: boolean, base: number, rate: number): number =>\n  applies ? base * rate : 0;\n\nconst surchargeForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item.type);\n  return (\n    conditionalAdjustment(item.cursed ?? false, base, CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE) +\n    conditionalAdjustment(\n      typeof item.enchantment === \"number\" && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n      base,\n      HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    )\n  );\n};\n\nconst insuredValueFor = (type: string): number => lookupValue(INSURANCE_VALUES, type);\n\nconst insuranceSumForItems = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuredValueFor(item.type), 0);\n\nconst basePremiumTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const quantityByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    quantityByType.set(item.type, (quantityByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  });\n\n  return Array.from(quantityByType.entries()).reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + basePremiumForGroup(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n};\n\nconst policyAdjustmentAmount = (\n  baseTotal: number,\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount = conditionalAdjustment(\n    customerYears >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD,\n    baseTotal,\n    LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE * baseTotal;\n  const followUpDiscount = conditionalAdjustment(\n    isFollowUp,\n    baseTotal,\n    FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE\n  );\n\n  return firstInsuranceSurcharge - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n};\n\nconst quoteForItems = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): { premium: number } => {\n  const baseTotal = basePremiumTotal(items);\n\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce(\n    (total, item) => total + surchargeForItem(item),\n    0\n  );\n\n  const policyBase = baseTotal + itemSurcharges;\n  const rawPremium =\n    policyBase + policyAdjustmentAmount(baseTotal, customerYears, isFollowUp) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(rawPremium) };\n};\n\nconst reimbursementForDamage = (policyItem: Item, damageAmount: number): number => {\n  const enchantment = typeof policyItem.enchantment === \"number\" ? policyItem.enchantment : 0;\n  const damageAfterEnchantmentReduction =\n    enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD\n      ? damageAmount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE\n      : damageAmount;\n  return Math.max(0, damageAfterEnchantmentReduction - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst capForPolicy = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems(items);\n\nconst quoteStepForPolicy = (steps: Step[], policyIndex: number): QuoteStep => {\n  const step = steps[policyIndex];\n  if (step.op !== \"quote\") {\n    throw new Error(`Policy ${policyIndex} is not a quote step`);\n  }\n  return step;\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>,\n  remainingCap: number\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const payoutBeforeCap = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    if (damage.amount < 0) {\n      throw new Error(\"Damage amount cannot be negative\");\n    }\n    const policyItem = policyItems.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!policyItem) {\n      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} not insured`);\n    }\n    return sum + reimbursementForDamage(policyItem, damage.amount);\n  }, 0);\n  const payout = Math.floor(Math.min(payoutBeforeCap, remainingCap));\n  return { payout, remainingCap: Math.floor(remainingCap - payout) };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> => {\n  const remainingCapByPolicy = new Map<number, number>();\n  return scenario.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFollowUp = index > 0;\n      return quoteForItems(step.items, scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFollowUp);\n    }\n    const policyStep = quoteStepForPolicy(scenario.steps, step.policy);\n    const cap = capForPolicy(policyStep.items);\n    const remainingCap = remainingCapByPolicy.get(step.policy) ?? cap;\n    const result = processClaim(policyStep.items, step.incident.damages, remainingCap);\n    remainingCapByPolicy.set(step.policy, result.remainingCap);\n    return result;\n  });\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944724750},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Basic quote premiums\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"oak\", enchantment: 1, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 93 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 49 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single moonstone -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Component block rules\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes without block discount -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 60 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote exactly 3 runes with block discount -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 198 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not mix different component types for the block discount -- 2 runes + 1 moonstone premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 88 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply separate blocks for each component type -- 3 runes + 3 moonstones premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 137 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should add cursed surcharge to a sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 165 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at level 5 -- premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges -- premium 195 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 195 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge below level 5 -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply first insurance surcharge -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on the second quote -- premium 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }, { premium: 100 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply item-specific modifiers per item and policy-wide modifiers on policy base -- cursed sword + plain amulet premium 231 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n            { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 231 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it(\"should compute newcomer with a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 165 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should compute long-standing customer's second contract -- premium 160 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }, { premium: 160 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Claim standard reimbursement\n  it(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G, remaining cap 1600 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should reimburse a rune damage minus deductible -- payout 100 G, remaining cap 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 33 }, { payout: 100, remainingCap: 400 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Claim special clauses\n  it(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage minus deductible -- payout 700 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 700, remainingCap: 1300 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should halve damage for enchantment level 9 or higher -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"magic surge\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply enchantment clause over dragon material when both apply -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply dragon-material clause when only it applies -- payout 700 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 700, remainingCap: 1300 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Multi-item / deductible\n  it(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident -- total payout 600 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false },\n            { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [\n              { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n              { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 },\n            ],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([\n      { premium: 181 },\n      { payout: 600, remainingCap: 2600 },\n    ]);\n  });\n  it(\"should sum insurance values for multiple items of the same type -- cap 4000 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false },\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 100 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 225 }, { payout: 0, remainingCap: 4000 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Cap exhaustion\n  it(\"should cap the first claim and track remaining cap -- first payout 1400 G, remaining 600 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 1400, remainingCap: 600 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should reduce the second claim by remaining cap -- second payout 600 G, remaining 0 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }],\n          },\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([\n      { premium: 115 },\n      { payout: 1400, remainingCap: 600 },\n      { payout: 600, remainingCap: 0 },\n    ]);\n  });\n\n  // Rounding\n  it(\"should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 7 runes with first insurance yields 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 198 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- high-enchantment damage 901 G yields 350 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"magic surge\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 901 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 350, remainingCap: 1650 }]);\n  });\n\n  // Error cases\n  it(\"should reject unknown item type in quote\", () => {\n    expect(() =>\n      processScenario({\n        customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        steps: [\n          {\n            op: \"quote\",\n            items: [{ type: \"broomstick\" }],\n          },\n        ],\n      })\n    ).toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"should reject unknown item type in claim\", () => {\n    expect(() =>\n      processScenario({\n        customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        steps: [\n          {\n            op: \"quote\",\n            items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n          },\n          {\n            op: \"claim\",\n            policy: 0,\n            incident: {\n              cause: \"fire\",\n              damages: [{ itemType: \"broomstick\", amount: 200 }],\n            },\n          },\n        ],\n      })\n    ).toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"should reject negative damage amount\", () => {\n    expect(() =>\n      processScenario({\n        customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        steps: [\n          {\n            op: \"quote\",\n            items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n          },\n          {\n            op: \"claim\",\n            policy: 0,\n            incident: {\n              cause: \"fire\",\n              damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: -200 }],\n            },\n          },\n        ],\n      })\n    ).toThrow();\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should reject more damages than insured items\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944724750},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the code. I have 38 passing tests and one it.todo. The code is for processing insurance quotes and claims for a fantasy claim office.\n\nLet me think about refactoring opportunities:\n\n1. Naming Evaluation:\n- `conditionalAdjustment` - takes `applies: boolean, base: number, rate: number` returns `applies ? base * rate : 0`. The name is okay but could be `applyRateWhen` or `rateAdjustmentIf`. It's a helper that applies a rate to a base if a condition is true. `conditionalAdjustment` is descriptive enough.\n- `policyAdjustmentAmount` - calculates the net adjustment from first insurance surcharge, loyalty discount, and follow-up discount. The name is a bit generic. It returns the amount to add to the policy base. Could be `policyModifierAmount` or `customerPolicyAdjustment`. But it's okay.\n- `quoteForItems` - returns `{ premium: number }`, maybe `quotePremiumForItems` would be more precise.\n- `processClaim` - processes a claim and returns payout and remainingCap. Maybe `settleClaim` would be more precise? `processClaim` is okay.\n- `quoteStepForPolicy` - finds the quote step for a given policy index. The name is a bit awkward. `quoteStepAt