quoteStepForPolicy` to `requireQuoteStepAt`.\n3. Extracted `reimbursementForDamageEntry` from `processClaim`.\n\nLet me consider if there's more to do. \n\nNow `processClaim` uses `sum(damages, ...)`. This is much cleaner.\n\nLet me look at `processScenario`:\n```ts\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> => {\n  const remainingCapByPolicy = new Map<number, number>();\n  return scenario.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFollowUp = index > 0;\n      return quoteForItems(step.items, scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFollowUp);\n    }\n    const policyStep = requireQuoteStepAt(scenario.steps, step.policy);\n    const cap = capForPolicy(policyStep.items);\n    const remainingCap = remainingCapByPolicy.get(step.policy) ?? cap;\n    const result = processClaim(policyStep.items, step.incident.damages, remainingCap);\n    remainingCapByPolicy.set(step.policy, result.remainingCap);\n    return result;\n  });\n};\n```\n\nThis is reasonably clear. Could extract `handleQuoteStep` and `handleClaimStep`, but that might be overkill. The current inline logic is readable.\n\nLet me think about Rule 4: Fewest Elements. We added `sum` and `reimbursementForDamageEntry`, but removed duplicate reduce patterns and cleaned up `processClaim`. Net effect is positive.\n\nLet me check if there are any other naming issues or duplication.\n\n- `basePremiumForItem` and `insuredValueFor` are thin wrappers around `lookupValue`. They reveal intent and are used multiple times. Keep them.\n- `capForPolicy` is a thin wrapper around `CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems`. It reveals intent. Keep it.\n- `basePremiumForGroup` handles component block pricing. Clear.\n\nPotential issue: `FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE` is always applied, which is misleading. But changing behavior is not refactoring. I could rename the constant to something more accurate, but that might affect external readers. Since tests call it \"first insurance surcharge\", I'll leave it.\n\nAnother potential issue: The `Item` interface has a `damage?: number` field, but I don't see it used anywhere. In `processClaim`, damages come from the claim step, not from the item. So `damage` on Item is unused. Could remove it (Rule 4). But is it used in tests? Let me check.\n\nTests create items with `damage`? Searching... no, tests don't set `damage` on items. They set `type`, `material`, `enchantment`, `cursed`. The `damage?: number` in Item interface is unused. Removing it would be a cleanup. But is it part of the domain model that might be used later? Since tests don't use it and the current code doesn't use it, removing it reduces elements. Let me check if it's exported or used elsewhere.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.grep:10","name":"grep","arguments":{"path":"src","pattern":"\\.damage","glob":"*.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":267,"output":718,"cacheRead":25600,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":688,"totalTokens":26585,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944771588,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-2a59c9d9-b1f1-4629-af0b-6e4ecabe39f5","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.grep:10","toolName":"grep","content":[{"type":"text","text":"claim-office.ts:206:     const result = processClaim(policyStep.items, step.incident.damages, remainingCap);"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944774845},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Only `step.incident.damages` uses `damages`, which is the claim step's damage array, not Item.damage. So `damage?: number` in Item is unused. I can remove it to reduce elements (Rule 4).\n\nBut wait, is `Item` exported? No, it's internal. Removing `damage?: number` won't break tests.\n\nLet me do that.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:11","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n  damage?: number;\n}\n","newText":"interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n}\n"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":68,"output":187,"cacheRead":26560,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":80,"totalTokens":26815,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944774846,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-92b4b031-7160-475b-8720-992d4eb5cfa0","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:11","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  36   type: string;\n  37   cursed?: boolean;\n  38   enchantment?: number;\n  39   material?: string;\n- 40   damage?: number;\n  41 }\n  42 \n  43 interface QuoteStep {\n  44   op: \"quote\";\n     ...","patch":"--- src/claim-office.ts\n+++ src/claim-office.ts\n@@ -36,9 +36,8 @@\n   type: string;\n   cursed?: boolean;\n   enchantment?: number;\n   material?: string;\n-  damage?: number;\n }\n \n interface QuoteStep {\n   op: \"quote\";\n","firstChangedLine":40},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944776010},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Run tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:12","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":93,"output":28,"cacheRead":26752,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4,"totalTokens":26873,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944776012,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-934d3238-40d3-46ca-a2d0-9533a67d6370","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:12","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-35-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (39 tests | 1 skipped) 8ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  38 passed | 1 todo (39)\n   Start at  01:59:37\n   Duration  208ms (transform 49ms, setup 0ms, collect 53ms, tests 8ms, environment 0ms, prepare 51ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944777481},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now let me read the final file and calculate APP mass.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:13","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":278,"output":35,"cacheRead":26816,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":15,"totalTokens":27129,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784944777482,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-c5178578-a841-4e51-b204-83737b34809e","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:13","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: {\n    cause: string;\n    damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>;\n  };\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\";\n\nconst lookupValue = (table: Record<string, number>, type: string): number => {\n  const value = table[type];\n  if (value === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n  }\n  return value;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (type: string): number => lookupValue(BASE_PREMIUMS, type);\n\nconst basePremiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  isComponent(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * basePremiumForItem(type);\n\nconst rateAdjustmentIf = (applies: boolean, base: number, rate: number): number =>\n  applies ? base * rate : 0;\n\nconst surchargeForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item.type);\n  return (\n    rateAdjustmentIf(item.cursed ?? false, base, CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE) +\n    rateAdjustmentIf(\n      typeof item.enchantment === \"number\" && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n      base,\n      HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    )\n  );\n};\n\nconst insuredValueFor = (type: string): number => lookupValue(INSURANCE_VALUES, type);\n\nconst sum = <T>(items: T[], getValue: (item: T) => number): number =>\n  items.reduce((total, item) => total + getValue(item), 0);\n\nconst insuranceSumForItems = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  sum(items, (item) => insuredValueFor(item.type));\n\nconst basePremiumTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const quantityByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  items.forEach((item) => {\n    quantityByType.set(item.type, (quantityByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  });\n\n  return sum(Array.from(quantityByType.entries()), ([type, count]) =>\n    basePremiumForGroup(type, count)\n  );\n};\n\nconst policyAdjustmentAmount = (\n  baseTotal: number,\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount = rateAdjustmentIf(\n    customerYears >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD,\n    baseTotal,\n    LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE * baseTotal;\n  const followUpDiscount = rateAdjustmentIf(\n    isFollowUp,\n    baseTotal,\n    FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE\n  );\n\n  return firstInsuranceSurcharge - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n};\n\nconst quoteForItems = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customerYears: number,\n  isFollowUp: boolean\n): { premium: number } => {\n  const baseTotal = basePremiumTotal(items);\n\n  const itemSurcharges = sum(items, surchargeForItem);\n\n  const policyBase = baseTotal + itemSurcharges;\n  const rawPremium =\n    policyBase + policyAdjustmentAmount(baseTotal, customerYears, isFollowUp) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(rawPremium) };\n};\n\nconst reimbursementForDamage = (policyItem: Item, damageAmount: number): number => {\n  const enchantment = typeof policyItem.enchantment === \"number\" ? policyItem.enchantment : 0;\n  const damageAfterEnchantmentReduction =\n    enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD\n      ? damageAmount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_REDUCTION_RATE\n      : damageAmount;\n  return Math.max(0, damageAfterEnchantmentReduction - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst reimbursementForDamageEntry = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damage: { itemType: string; amount: number }\n): number => {\n  if (damage.amount < 0) {\n    throw new Error(\"Damage amount cannot be negative\");\n  }\n  const policyItem = policyItems.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n  if (!policyItem) {\n    throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} not insured`);\n  }\n  return reimbursementForDamage(policyItem, damage.amount);\n};\n\nconst capForPolicy = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSumForItems(items);\n\nconst requireQuoteStepAt = (steps: Step[], policyIndex: number): QuoteStep => {\n  const step = steps[policyIndex];\n  if (step.op !== \"quote\") {\n    throw new Error(`Policy ${policyIndex} is not a quote step`);\n  }\n  return step;\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }>,\n  remainingCap: number\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const payoutBeforeCap = sum(damages, (damage) =>\n    reimbursementForDamageEntry(policyItems, damage)\n  );\n  const payout = Math.floor(Math.min(payoutBeforeCap, remainingCap));\n  return { payout, remainingCap: Math.floor(remainingCap - payout) };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> => {\n  const remainingCapByPolicy = new Map<number, number>();\n  return scenario.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFollowUp = index > 0;\n      return quoteForItems(step.items, scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFollowUp);\n    }\n    const policyStep = requireQuoteStepAt(scenario.steps, step.policy);\n    const cap = capForPolicy(policyStep.items);\n    const remainingCap = remainingCapByPolicy.get(step.policy) ?? cap;\n    const result = processClaim(policyStep.items, step.incident.damages, remainingCap);\n    remainingCapByPolicy.set(step.policy, result.remainingCap);\n    return result;\n  });\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784944778398},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me think about whether there's more refactoring to do. The code looks cleaner now. Let me consider a few more things:\n\n1. `policyAdjustmentAmount` - the name is fine. But the fact that first insurance surcharge is unconditional is still a bit odd. No change.\n\n2. `quoteForItems` - uses `policyAdjustmentAmount(baseTotal, customerYears, isFollowUp)`. Good.\n\n3. `processScenario` - the claim branch is clear. The `remainingCapByPolicy` map is used to track remaining caps across claims. Good.\n\n4. Could I use `sum` in `processScenario`? No.\n\n5. Could I extract `handleQuoteStep` and `handleClaimStep`? It might improve `processScenario` readability but adds functions. The current inline logic is straightforward. I'll leave it.\n\n6. Could I simplify `reimbursementForDamage`? It uses a ternary for enchantment reduction. That's clear.\n\n7. Could I use `sum` in `basePremiumTotal` for the forEach? No, because we're building a Map.\n\n8. The `forEach` in `basePremiumTotal` could be replaced with a reduce, but that might be less clear. Keep it.\n\nI think I've done enough. Let me now do the APP mass calculation.\n\nI need to calculate mass before and after. I already did rough calculations for the specific changes. But the instructions say to calculate APP mass before and after refactoring. I'll do a whole-file calculation, but it will be approximate.\n\nActually, since the changes are spread across multiple functions, let me calculate mass for the entire file before and after. I'll be systematic but approximate. I'll count:\n- Constants\n- Bindings (parameters, variables declared with const/let)\n- Invocations (function/method calls including operators like `+`, `*`, etc